hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"5401","Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us; al-Hasan ibn 'Ali ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Waqid, from Marwan ibn al-Muqa'', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke his fast, he said: Thirst has gone, the veins are moistened, and the reward is confirmed, if Allah wills. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain with this isnad."
"5402","And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Rabi'ah al-Kilabi narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Makkah, he said: O Allah, do not decree our deaths here until You have brought us out of it."
"5403","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us; 'Uthman ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Harrani narrated to us; 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abu al-'Awwam, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn Musahiq, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: You will form armies. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, choose for me. He said: Upon you is al-Sham, for it is Allah's choicest land; in it are Allah's best servants. Whoever dislikes that, let him join his Najd, for Allah has guaranteed al-Sham and its people for me. And this hadith - we do not know it narrated from Ibn 'Umar except through this chain with this isnad."
"5404","Sulayman ibn Sayf al-Harrani narrated to us; Abu 'Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us; 'Abbad narrated to us [...] Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to me; 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited this verse upon the pulpit: And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves, until he finished the verse reaching: Glory be to Him, Exalted above what they associate. He said: The pulpit shook like this, moving back and forth three times. And this hadith was narrated from Ibn 'Umar by 'Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam and Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir; and 'Ubaydullah ibn Miqsam added: It kept moving back and forth until we said: It will surely fall with him."
"5405","Sulayman ibn Sayf narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us; Abu Bakr ibn Badr narrated to us, he said: I heard Maymun ibn Mihran narrating, he said: I heard Ibn 'Umar saying: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trimming his mustache closely."
"5406","Muhammad ibn 'Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us; Abu Nu'aym narrated to us; Sharik narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn 'Isa, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy will not be shown mercy. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn 'Umar except 'Atiyyah, nor from 'Atiyyah except 'Abdullah ibn 'Isa, nor from 'Abdullah ibn 'Isa except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Abu Nu'aym."
"5407","Ahmad ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Husayn narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Shabib narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn 'Isa narrated to us, from 'Atiyyah, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The slave woman is divorced with two divorces, and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles. And this hadith - we do not know anyone who narrated it except 'Umar ibn Shabib."
"5408","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Baylamani narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nuh fasted the white days, and they are: the thirteenth, the fourteenth, and the fifteenth."
"5409","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pardon one another and grudges between you will fall away."
"5410","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said regarding slaves: If they do well, accept it; if they do badly, pardon; and if they overpower you, sell them."
"5411","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no preemption (shuf'ah) for one absent or for a minor; preemption is like untying a hobble."
"5412","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prayer of sword-fighting (in battle) is one rak'ah in whatever manner; it suffices a man. When - I think he said - he does that, he does not repeat."
"5413","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever mutilates his slave, he is free, and he is the freedman of Allah and His Messenger."
"5414","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A granted benefit (minhah) is to be returned, and people are bound by their stipulations so long as they accord with the truth."
"5415","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The crying out of a newborn child is sneezing."
"5416","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us: Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cursed is whoever affiliates himself to other than his patrons; cursed is whoever claims (descent) to other than his father; and cursed is whoever alters the landmarks of the land."
"5417","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us; Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing praying in a single garment; so I stood on his left, and he turned me until he placed me on his right. Abu Bakr said: The hadiths of Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman from his father from Ibn 'Umar are numerous, and they contain many objectionable (munkar) reports; we have only brought out from them what is fit to bring out, for Muhammad is weak in hadith according to the people of knowledge."
"5418","Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us; Muhammad ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: War is deceit. Muhammad ibn al-Harith - 'Affan narrated from him, and he is a well-known man with nothing wrong with him; the objectionable character of these hadiths comes only from Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman."
"5419","Al-Hasan ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz al-Jarawi and Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar."
"5420","And 'Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated it to us; Yahya al-Wuhazi narrated to us; 'Abdullah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When you see the praise-mongers, throw dust in their faces. And this hadith was narrated by Zayd ibn Aslam from Ibn 'Umar, and 'Ata ibn Abi Rabah narrated it from Ibn 'Umar; and we do not know it narrated from Ibn 'Umar except through these two chains. Abu 'Abdullah narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ayyub informed me, he said: Abu Bakr dictated to me, he said: These hadiths of Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar were narrated by 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, and more than one narrator followed 'Ubaydullah in his narration from Nafi'; so we mentioned some of those who followed him in his narration from Nafi', for he narrated most extensively in sequence from Nafi', so we began with him, then mentioned what 'Ubaydullah did not narrate and what others narrated afterwards."
"5421","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make the last of your prayers witr."
"5422","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim man who has something to bequeath should spend two nights except that his will is written with him."
"5423","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No man who has wealth he wishes to bequeath should spend two nights except that his will is written with him."
"5424","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5425","And Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated it to us; Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated to us, from Ibn 'Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I think it is from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5426","And Muhammad ibn Harb narrated it to us; 'Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: It is part of a Muslim's right that he not spend two nights without writing his will."
"5427","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Perform part of your prayers in your houses, and do not take them as graves."
"5428","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in your houses, and do not take them as graves."
"5429","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5430","And Ahmad ibn Malik narrated it to us; 'Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade continuous fasting (wisal). They said: You fast continuously, O Messenger of Allah!! He said: I am not like any of you; I spend the night fed and given drink."
"5431","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us; Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated it, and 'Umar ibn Shaybah also narrated it from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar; so we sufficed with those we named."
"5432","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah; Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I never abandoned touching these two corners - the Yamani and the (Black) Stone - since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching them, in hardship or ease."
"5433","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us; 'Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And this hadith was narrated by Ibn Abi Rawwad and others from Nafi', following those we named."
"5434","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, that when travel pressed him, he would combine Maghrib and 'Isha after the twilight disappeared, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him, would combine Maghrib and 'Isha."
"5435","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Abu 'Asim narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5436","And 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated it to us; Ibn Fudayl narrated to us; my father narrated to us, from Nafi', and 'Abdullah ibn Waqid, they said: The urgent news of Safiyyah reached Ibn 'Umar at sunset, so he said to the mu'adhdhin: (Delay) the prayer. He said: Proceed. He traveled until before the twilight disappeared; he dismounted and prayed Maghrib, then waited until the twilight disappeared, then prayed 'Isha, then said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when an urgent matter pressed him, would do as I did; and on that day and night he traveled a three-day journey."
"5437","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman narrated it to us; 'Ubaydullah - meaning Ibn Musa - narrated to us; Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when travel pressed him, would combine Maghrib and 'Isha."
"5438","And Ibn Karamah narrated it to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Isra'il, from Khusayf, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when travel pressed him, he would delay Zuhr and hasten 'Asr, and delay Maghrib and hasten 'Isha. And a group whom we did not name narrated this hadith from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar."
"5439","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab ibn 'Abd al-Majid narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly - regarding hastening the prayer."
"5440","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah; Nafi' informed me that 'Abdullah ibn 'Abdullah and Salim ibn 'Abdullah spoke to 'Abdullah when there was strife between al-Hajjaj and Ibn al-Zubayr, saying: It will not harm you to skip hajj this year, for we fear there will be fighting among the people or you will be prevented from the House. He said: If I am prevented from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did when the disbelievers of Quraysh prevented him from the House: I call you to witness that I have obligated an 'umrah upon myself. He set out until he reached Dhu al-Hulayfah and entered ihram for 'umrah, then said: If I am prevented from it, I will do as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did while I was with him. Then he recited: You have in the Messenger of Allah a good example. Then he traveled until, at the back of al-Bayda, he said: Their matter is one; if I am prevented from 'umrah, I will be prevented from hajj. I call you to witness that I have obligated a hajj along with my 'umrah. He set out until he purchased a sacrificial animal at Qudayd, then performed one tawaf of the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwah for both, and did not exit ihram from them until the Day of Sacrifice. And this hadith was narrated by Musa ibn 'Uqbah, Ibn 'Ajlan, Malik, and a group from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar; so we sufficed with those we mentioned."
"5441","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I learned the talbiyah from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, You have no partner, here I am; indeed praise, favor, and dominion belong to You; You have no partner."
"5442","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I received it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And in another place: I learned it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned similarly."
"5443","Abu Sa'id 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us; Abu Khalid - meaning al-Ahmar - narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting the talbiyah: Here I am, O Allah, here I am; here I am, You have no partner ... and he mentioned similarly. And this hadith was narrated by Malik, Ibn Abi Layla, and more than one; so we sufficed with those we mentioned."
"5444","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah; Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) held a race between trained horses from al-Hafya to Thaniyyat al-Wada', and between untrained ones from Thaniyyat al-Wada' to the mosque of Banu Zurayq."
"5445","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5446","And Mu'ammal narrated it to us; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raced horses: he sent the trained ones from al-Hafya to Thaniyyat al-Wada', and sent the untrained ones from Thaniyyat al-Wada' to the mosque of Banu Zurayq. And this hadith was narrated by Sakhr ibn Juwayrah, Malik, Musa ibn 'Uqbah, Juwayriyah ibn Asma, and others; so we sufficed with those we named."
"5447","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Those who make these images will be punished on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said to them: Give life to what you created."
"5448","And Wahb ibn Yahya narrated it to us; Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us; 'Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Those who make images are the most severely punished people on the Day of Resurrection; it will be said: Give life to what you created."
"5449","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And this hadith was narrated by more than one whom we did not name; we sufficed with those we mentioned."
"5450","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the night prayer. He said: One of you prays two by two; when he fears dawn, he prays one rak'ah making his prayer odd-numbered."
"5451","And Muhammad ibn Mirdas al-Ansari narrated it to us; Sulayman ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two by two, and witr is one rak'ah. The hadith of Sulayman al-Taymi was narrated by others besides Sulayman ibn Sulayman, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Tawus, from Ibn 'Umar."
"5452","And Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us; Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah and Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The night prayer is two rak'ahs; when you fear dawn, make it odd with one."
"5453","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The night prayer is two by two; when one of you fears dawn, he prays one rak'ah making his prayer odd-numbered."
"5454","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5455","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The night prayer is two by two; when one of you fears dawn, he prays one rak'ah making his prayer odd-numbered."
"5456","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five animals - there is no sin upon one who kills them even while in ihram: the scorpion, the kite, the vicious dog, the crow, and the mouse."
"5457","Sulayman ibn Khallad narrated to us; Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly - meaning regarding what the muhrim kills."
"5458","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet, upon him be peace, similarly."
"5459","And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us; Isma'il - meaning Ibn 'Ulayyah - narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Five animals - there is no sin upon the muhrim for killing them: the kite, the scorpion, the mouse, the crow, and the vicious dog."
"5460","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah; Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade milking livestock without the permission of their owners."
"5461","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5462","And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us; Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"5463","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: None of you should milk his brother's livestock. Would any of you like his storeroom to be approached and its door broken?! None of you should milk anyone's livestock except with his permission."
"5464","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Abu 'Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: None of you should milk anyone's livestock without his permission. Would any of you like his storeroom to be approached and the door of his treasury broken and its contents scattered?! Their animals' udders are but storehouses for them; so none should milk anyone's livestock except with his permission."
"5465","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever misses the 'Asr prayer, it is as if his family and wealth were destroyed."
"5466","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated it to us; 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Shayban, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5467","And 'Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated it to us; Ibn Fudayl narrated to us; Layth and al-Hajjaj ibn Artah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever misses the 'Asr prayer. And Shayban said: Whoever abandons the 'Asr prayer until it escapes him, it is as if his family and wealth were destroyed."
"5468","And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated it to us; Bishr ibn 'Umar narrated to us; al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one who misses the 'Asr prayer, it is as if his family and wealth were destroyed."
"5469","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated it to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5470","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5471","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, he said: A man asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the lizard (dabb). He said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it."
"5472","And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5473","And Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated it to us; 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was asked about the lizard (dabb) and said: I do not eat it, nor do I forbid it."
"5474","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us; Sa'id - meaning Ibn Abi 'Arubah - narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Hakim, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5475","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that a lizard (dabb) was brought to him; he neither ate it nor forbade it."
"5476","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah; Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) obligated zakat al-fitr upon the young and the old, the free and the slave."
"5477","And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us; Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us; Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5478","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Qabisah narrated to us; Sufyan narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5479","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5480","And 'Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Nafi', from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly, except that he said: Upon the young and the old, the free and the slave among the Muslims."
"5481","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"5482","And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us; Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5483","And Ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us; Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly regarding the story of fitr. As for the hadith of Malik from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in which he mentioned: among the Muslims - Isma'il ibn Ja'far followed him in his narration, from 'Umar ibn Nafi', from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the hadith of Ya'la from Muhammad ibn Ishaq from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar does not mention: among the Muslims."
"5484","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the Muslim man is obedience in what he loves and hates, except that he be commanded to disobey; when he is commanded to disobey, there is no obedience."
"5485","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us; Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated this hadith from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar, similarly."
"5486","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah; Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, he said - and I know it only to be from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful."
"5487","And Abu Kamil and Yahya ibn Durust narrated it to us, they said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is wine, and every intoxicant is unlawful; and whoever drinks wine in this world and dies addicted to it will not drink it in the Hereafter."
"5488","And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated it to us; my father narrated to us, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"5489","And Ibn Karamah narrated it to us; 'Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Shayban, from Layth, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every intoxicant is unlawful, and every intoxicant is wine. And Muhammad ibn Ishaq, Musa ibn 'Uqbah, and others narrated this hadith."
"5490","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A man should not propose over the proposal of his brother, nor sell over the sale of his brother, except that he give him permission."
"5491","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us; Rawh narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: None of you should sell over the sale of another, nor should one of you propose over the proposal of another. And more than one narrated this hadith, among them Malik, Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah, and others."
"5492","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, they said: Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah; Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines."
"5493","Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq informed me; Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5494","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When one of you dies, his seat is presented to him morning and evening; if he is of the people of Paradise, then of the people of Paradise; if he is of the people of Fire, then of the people of Fire. It is said: This is your seat until you are resurrected."
"5495","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5496","And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us; my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly."
"5497","And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us; Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5498","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated it to us; Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dies, his place is presented to him morning and evening; if he is of the people of Paradise, then of the people of Paradise; if he is of the people of Fire, then of the people of Fire. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Nafi'; we mentioned the hadith of Ayyub and the hadith of 'Ubaydullah."
"5499","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya and 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"5500","Wahb ibn Yahya narrated to us; Maymun ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Muhammad and 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever bears arms against us is not of us."
"5501","And Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari narrated to us; Sa'id ibn Sulayman narrated to us; Ayyub ibn 'Utbah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The example of the companion of the Qur'an is like tied camels; if its owner hobbles it, he holds it; if he releases it, it goes away."
"5502","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh narrated to us; Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The example of the companion of the Qur'an is but like tied camels; if he tends to it, he retains it; if he leaves it, it goes away."
"5503","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Abu 'Amir narrated to us; Hisham ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly. And he added in it: The companion of the Qur'an, if he recites it, remembers it; if he abandons it, forgets it."
"5504","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us; Rawh ibn 'Ubadah narrated to us; 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), similarly to the hadith of 'Ubaydullah."
"5505","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, he said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"5506","And Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us; 'Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us; Ma'mar informed me, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade shighar."
"5507","Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik ibn Abi al-Shawarib narrated to us; Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Rahman al-Sarraj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade shighar. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Nafi'."
"5508","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya and 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us - and the wording is Yahya's: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting (caravans in advance)."
"5509","And Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated it to us; Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us; Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from 'Umar ibn Nafi', from his father, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade meeting riders (before the market), selling of a town-dweller for a Bedouin, and najsh (false bidding)."
"5510","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us; Yahya narrated to us, from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the meat of domestic donkeys."
"5511","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated: from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade eating the domestic donkey, though they had been in need of it on the day of Khaybar."
"5512","'Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi' and Salim, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys on the day of Khaybar."
"5513","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya and 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, who said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever buys food must not sell it until he has taken full possession of it."
"5514","Wahb ibn Yahya narrated to us: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated: from 'Umar ibn Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5515","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: Malik narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever purchases food must not sell it until he has taken full possession of it. And this hadith was also narrated by Musa ibn 'Uqbah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar."
"5516","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, who said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers anywhere else except the Sacred Mosque."
"5517","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: Musa al-Juhani narrated, who said: I heard Nafi' narrating from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5518","Wahb ibn Yahya narrated to us: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated: 'Umar ibn Muhammad narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers elsewhere among the mosques except the Sacred Mosque."
"5519","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, who said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees."
"5520","Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us: Abu Ahmad narrated: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the like of it."
"5521","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: A man's prayer in congregation exceeds his prayer alone by twenty-seven degrees."
"5522","And Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-Malik narrated to us: Abu Sadaqah Bakr ibn Sadaqah al-Hadani narrated: Ibn 'Ajlan narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The congregational prayer surpasses a man's prayer alone by some twenty prayers."
"5523","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that people used to trade food in bulk by estimation, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them to sell it until they moved it, meaning to their own lodgings."
"5524","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The believer's dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"5525","Wahb ibn Yahya narrated to us: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated: from 'Umar ibn Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer's dream is one part of seventy parts of prophethood."
"5526","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: 'Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), as I reckon, with a similar narration."
"5527","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, who said: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he stood at the door of 'A'ishah or Hafsah - Abu Musa doubted - and said: Tribulation is from here, from where the horn of Satan rises, two or three times."
"5528","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated: from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood facing the east at the chamber of 'A'ishah and said: Tribulation is from here, saying it twice: from where the horn of Satan rises."
"5529","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated: my father narrated to me: from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5530","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When a slave is sincere to his master and performs the worship of his Lord well, he has his reward twice over."
"5531","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated: Sa'id ibn Zayd narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5532","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: Malik narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration. And the hadith of Ayyub - we know of no one who narrated it from Ayyub from Nafi' except Sa'id ibn Zayd, and Sa'id ibn Zayd is righteous."
"5533","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya and 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from 'Abdullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: You will surely fight the Jews, until even a stone says: O Muslim, this is a Jew, come and kill him. And 'Abd al-Wahhab said: This is a Jew behind me."
"5534","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated: from his father, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5535","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered Mecca from the upper pass and left by the lower one."
"5536","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated: Ayyub narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The upper hand is better than the lower hand; the upper hand is the giving one and the lower hand is the begging one."
"5537","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off the hand for a shield worth three dirhams."
"5538","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated: Ayyub narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5539","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated: from Hanzalah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he cut off the hand for a shield valued at three dirhams."
"5540","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: Malik narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off the hand of a thief for a shield. And this hadith was also narrated by Musa ibn 'Uqbah from Nafi'."
"5541","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he cursed the woman who tattoos and the woman who has herself tattooed, and the woman who joins hair and the woman who has it joined for her."
"5542","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Ahead of you is a Basin as between Jarba' and Adhruh."
"5543","And al-'Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Narsi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5544","And Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated: from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Ahead of you is a Basin from such-and-such to such-and-such - al-Fudayl doubted, while Hammad did not doubt. A man in Nafi''s presence said that he doubted, and he said: It is true, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5545","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya and 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Fever is from the heat of Hell, so cool it with water. And 'Abd al-Wahhab said: Extinguish it with water."
"5546","And Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us: 'Isa ibn Yunus narrated: from al-Awza'i, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5547","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya and 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The two parties to a sale each have the choice in their sale until they part, unless the sale is with a stipulated choice. Nafi' said: When Ibn 'Umar bought something he liked, he would part from his companion."
"5548","And Abu Kamil narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sellers each have the choice as long as they have not parted."
"5549","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated: from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5550","Abu 'Asim narrated: 'Umar ibn Muhammad narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said the hadith: and the sale may be with a stipulated choice."
"5551","And al-Hasan ibn 'Arafah narrated to us: ... narrated ... from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration. The hadith of 'Umar ibn Muhammad ..."
"5552","... Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated: from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet ... Muhammad."
"5553","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried out li'an between a man and his wife of the Ansar and separated them."
"5554","And Muhammad narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The son of 'Abdullah ibn Ubayy came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when his father died and said: Give us your shirt. So he gave him his shirt and said: When you finish, inform me. When he was about to pray over him, 'Umar pulled him and said: Has Allah not forbidden you regarding the hypocrites? He said: I am between two options; He said: Ask forgiveness for them or do not ask forgiveness for them. So he prayed over him, then Allah sent down: And never pray over any of them who dies, nor stand by his grave. So he stopped praying over them."
"5555","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5556","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5557","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: from Malik, from Nafi' and Zayd ibn Aslam and 'Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever drags his garment out of pride, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection."
"5558","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from the mosques."
"5559","Mu'ammal narrated to us: Isma'il narrated: Ayyub narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not prevent the female servants of Allah from praying in the mosques."
"5560","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed the name 'Asiyah and said: You are Jamilah. And this hadith - we know of no one who narrated it from 'Ubaydullah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar except Yahya ibn Sa'id and Hammad ibn Salamah."
"5561","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit Quba' riding and walking."
"5562","And Ahmad ibn Sinan narrated to us: Asbat narrated: Muhammad ibn 'Ajlan narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit Quba' riding and walking."
"5563","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: No woman should travel for three days except with a mahram."
"5564","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The people of the pre-Islamic age used to sell camel meat on credit until habal al-habalah - and habal al-habalah is when the she-camel gives birth to what is in her belly and then carries again - so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade them."
"5565","Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who reported that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of habal al-habalah, meaning the offspring of the offspring."
"5566","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated: 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated: from his father, from Ibn 'Umar."
"5567","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: from Malik and Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade the sale of habal al-habalah."
"5568","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding: On the Day when mankind will stand before the Lord of the worlds - he said: Until one of them stands in his sweat up to the middle of his ears."
"5569","And Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-'Aqadi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5570","And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: 'Isa ibn Yunus and Abu Usamah narrated: from Ibn 'Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration to the hadith of Yahya from 'Ubaydullah. And this hadith - we know of no one who transmitted it attributed from Ayyub except Hammad, nor do we know of anyone who transmitted it attributed from Ibn 'Awn except 'Isa ibn Yunus and Abu Usamah."
"5571","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated: my father narrated to me: from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5572","And Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated: from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration to the hadith of Ayyub and Ibn 'Awn."
"5573","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let the beards grow and trim the mustaches."
"5574","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Two persons must not hold a secret conversation to the exclusion of their companion."
"5575","Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated: from 'Abdullah ibn 'Amir, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When there are three, two must not converse privately to the exclusion of the third."
"5576","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5577","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said during the Khaybar expedition: Whoever eats of this plant - meaning garlic - must not come to the mosque. Or he said: a mosque."
"5578","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that a spear used to be planted for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he would pray toward it."
"5579","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when it was a rainy night, would order a caller to announce after the adhan: the prayer is in the lodgings."
"5580","Ahmad ibn Aban narrated to us: Sufyan narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5581","'Ali ibn Ishkab narrated to us: Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated: from Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that he found severe cold one night, so he ordered the muezzin, who called the adhan with those with him, and said: Pray in your lodgings, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when it was like this, would order the people to pray in their lodgings."
"5582","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted al-'Abbas to spend the nights of Mina in Mecca on account of the water service."
"5583","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten? He said: May Allah have mercy on those who shave. They said: And those who shorten? He said on the fourth: And those who shorten."
"5584","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Rawh narrated: from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5585","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he returned from armies, expeditions, Hajj or 'Umrah, would ascend an elevation and say three times: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner; to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, and He is over all things capable. Returning, repentant, worshipping, praising our Lord. There is no god but Allah alone; He fulfilled His promise and defeated the Confederates alone."
"5586","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, what clothes do we wear when we enter ihram? He said: Do not wear shirts, trousers, or leather socks, unless one of you finds no sandals, then let him cut them below the ankles; nor any garment touched by wars or saffron."
"5587","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: 'Uthman ibn 'Umar narrated: Ibn 'Awn narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"5588","And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"5589","And Sulayman ibn 'Ubaydullah al-Ghaylani narrated to us: Abu Qutaybah narrated: Shu'bah narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that a man called out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): What clothes does the muhrim wear? He said: Do not wear shirts, turbans, trousers, hooded cloaks, or leather socks, unless there are no sandals, then socks cut below the ankles; nor a garment dyed with wars or saffron. And the wording is the wording of 'Abdullah ibn 'Awn; and the hadith of Shu'bah - we know of no one who narrated it from Shu'bah except Abu Qutaybah."
"5590","Bishr ibn Khalaf narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated: Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration to the hadith of Ayyub."
"5591","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration to the hadith of Ayyub."
"5592","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The month is like this and like this and like this - joining his ten fingers twice and folding the thumb on the third - and do not fast until you see it, nor break the fast until you see it; if it is obscured from you, then estimate for it."
"5593","Mu'ammal narrated to us: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The month is twenty-nine, so do not fast until you see it, nor break the fast until you see it."
"5594","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from 'Abdullah ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night at Dhu Tuwa, and when morning came he entered Mecca."
"5595","And 'Amr narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade traveling with the Qur'an to enemy land for fear they would seize it."
"5596","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: Ayyub narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5597","And al-Husayn ibn 'Abbad narrated to us: Muslim narrated: from Shu'bah, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5598","And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated: from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade traveling with the Qur'an to enemy land."
"5599","And Sa'dan ibn Nasr narrated to us: Musa ibn Dawud narrated: Zuhayr narrated: from Yahya ibn Sa'id and Musa ibn 'Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade traveling with the Qur'an to enemy land, and I think he said: for fear the enemy would seize it."
"5600","'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Bilal calls the adhan at night, so eat and drink until Ibn Umm Maktum calls the adhan."
"5601","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that men and women used to perform ablution in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from a single vessel."
"5602","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"5603","And Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated to us: 'Umar ibn 'Ali narrated: al-Hajjaj narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I saw men and women in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution from a single vessel."
"5604","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated: from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, with a similar narration."
"5605","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a share in a slave has freed him; if he has wealth covering his price, he is freed entirely from his wealth."
"5606","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us, both saying: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever frees his portion or share in a slave, and has wealth covering his price at a fair valuation, he is freed entirely from his wealth; otherwise, what has been freed of him is freed."
"5607","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: from Rawh, from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Whoever frees a share of his in a slave, and has what covers the price of the slave, it is assessed at a fair value, then he gives his partners their portions - he is freed at his expense; otherwise, what has been freed of him is freed."
"5608","'Ubayd ibn Isma'il al-Habbari narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter unless he repents."
"5609","And 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that Hafsah said: O Messenger of Allah, why have people exited ihram while you have not exited your 'umrah? He said: I have matted my hair, so I will not exit ihram until I sacrifice."
"5610","Nasr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Kathir ibn Hisham narrated: Ja'far ibn Burqan narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that Hafsah said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... and he mentioned a similar narration."
"5611","And 'Ubayd narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assigned two shares to the horse and one share to the foot soldier."
"5612","And Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us: Sulaym ibn Akhdar informed us: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed the spoils on the day of Hunayn: two shares to the horse and one share to its rider."
"5613","And 'Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: Whoever calls his brother a disbeliever, one of them has incurred it."
"5614","And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated: my father and Raqabah narrated to me: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5615","'Ubayd ibn Isma'il narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever vows to obey Allah must obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Allah must not disobey Him. And this hadith - I fear Abu Usamah erred in it, for Ibn Idris narrates it from 'Ubaydullah from Talhah ibn 'Abd al-Malik from al-Qasim from 'A'ishah, and that is correct in my view."
"5616","And Abu al-Sa'ib Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not fast on the day of 'Arafah, nor Abu Bakr, nor 'Umar."
"5617","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated: Sufyan narrated: from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration. And this hadith - we know of it from Ibn 'Umar only through these two routes we mentioned."
"5618","And 'Abdullah ibn Sa'id and Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, both saying: Abu Usamah narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed one of the two afternoon prayers and erred, saluting after two rak'ahs. A man called Dhu al-Yadayn said to him: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: Neither happened - until he verified, then he prayed the remainder of his prayer and prostrated twice ... and he mentioned a narration similar to the hadith of Ibn 'Awn and Hisham from Muhammad from Abu Hurayrah on the story of Dhu al-Yadayn. And this hadith - we know of no one who narrated it from 'Ubaydullah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar except Abu Usamah."
"5619","Yahya ibn Habib ibn 'Arabi narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated: from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver two sermons, separating them with a sitting."
"5620","Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray at the rising of the sun nor at its setting."
"5621","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Intense heat is from the heat of Hell. And this hadith - we know of no one who narrated it from 'Ubaydullah from Nafi' from Ibn 'Umar except 'Abd al-Wahhab."
"5622","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar - may Allah forgive it; and Aslam - may Allah grant it peace."
"5623","Al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated: my father narrated to me: from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the pulpit: Ghifar - may Allah forgive it; Aslam - may Allah grant it peace; and 'Usayyah - it disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"5624","And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated; and Ahmad ibn 'Abdah narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hypocrite is like a stray sheep between two flocks, going to these once and to those once, not knowing which to follow."
"5625","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The hypocrite is like a stray sheep between two flocks, turning to this one once and to that one another time, not knowing which to follow."
"5626","And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us: Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated: my father narrated to me: from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5627","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: narrated from 'Abd al-Wahhab: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Uhud when I was fourteen years old, and he deemed me too young and sent me back with the boys; then on the day of the Trench I was presented to him when I was fifteen and he permitted me."
"5628","And Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us: Yazid ibn Harun narrated: Abu Ma'shar informed us: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I was presented to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was thirteen and he did not accept me; I was presented to him when I was fourteen and he did not accept me; and I was presented to him when I was fifteen and he permitted me."
"5629","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: 'Abd al-Wahhab narrated: from 'Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the False Messiah and said: Your Lord is not one-eyed; the False Messiah is one-eyed, his right eye as though a protruding grape."
"5630","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us: Yahya narrated: from 'Ubaydullah: Nafi' informed me, from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer must bathe."
"5631","And 'Amr ibn 'Ali narrated to us: Ibn Abi 'Adi narrated: from Shu'bah, from al-Hakam, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever comes to Friday prayer must bathe."
"5632","Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated: Shu'bah narrated: from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"5633","And Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us: 'Abd al-Rahman narrated: from Malik, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with a similar narration."
"5634","And Bishr ibn Khalid al-'Askari narrated to us: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated: from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5635","And Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated: Musa ibn 'Uqbah narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5636","And Muhammad ibn 'Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah narrated: Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5637","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar and Muhammad ibn Karamah narrated to us, both saying: 'Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated: from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5638","And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated: Ibn 'Awn narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5639","And Ahmad ibn Mansur narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated: from Abu Shihab, from Yunus, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5640","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated: al-Ajlah narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he said on the pulpit ..."
"5641","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Ya'la ibn 'Ubayd narrated: 'Uthman ibn Hakim narrated."
"5642","And 'Abd al-Warith ibn 'Abd al-Samad narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Khalifah ibn Ghalib narrated, both from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching on the pulpit ..."
"5643","And al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us: 'Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Asma' narrated: Juwayriyah ibn Asma' narrated."
"5644","And Wahb ibn Yahya al-Qaysi narrated to us: Maymun ibn Zayd narrated: 'Umar ibn Muhammad narrated ..."
"5645","And Ahmad ibn al-Faraj narrated to us: Abu Haywah Shurayh ibn Yazid narrated: Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated."
"5646","And Ma'mar ibn Sahl narrated to us: Malik ibn Isma'il narrated: Isra'il narrated: from Jabir ..."
"5647","And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us: Jarir narrated: from Layth, meaning Ibn Abi Sulaym."
"5648","Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad and al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, both saying: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated: Hisham ibn al-Ghaz narrated - all of them from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah, blessed and exalted, has a right upon every Muslim to bathe one day every seven days, and if he has perfume to apply it. And this wording is that of Shababah alone from Hisham."
"5649","Muhammad ibn 'Ubaydullah ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar."
"5650","And Muhammad ibn Musa al-Qattan narrated to us: Bishr ibn Mubashshir narrated: al-Hakam ibn Fudayl narrated: from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Nafi' ..."
"5651","And 'Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Salih narrated: Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi' ..."
"5652","And Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us: Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated: 'Uthman ibn Waqid narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he said: Whoever of you comes to Friday prayer must bathe."
"5653","And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated: Mansur ibn Dinar narrated, who said: I asked Nafi' about bathing on Friday, and he said: Ibn 'Umar said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever comes to Friday prayer must bathe."
"5654","Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us: Abu 'Asim narrated: 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated: from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer must bathe."
"5655","And Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us: Asad ibn Musa narrated: Isra'il narrated: from Abu Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn 'Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer must bathe."
"5656","5647 - Al-Hasan ibn Hammad ibn Anbasah al-Warraq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, meaning Ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Nafi'."
"5657","5648 - And al-Hasan ibn Hammad narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Sabiq narrated to us, that he said: Whoever comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Mansur except Ibrahim ibn Tahman, and we do not know that Mansur transmitted as musnad from Nafi' from Ibn Umar any hadith other than this one."
"5658","5649 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, Ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, Asim ibn Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from his brother Zayd ibn Muhammad and Waqid ibn Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl."
"5659","5650 - Al-Hasan ibn Khalaf al-Wasiti narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yusuf al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Muthanna, meaning Ibn al-Sabbah, narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5660","5651 - Al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Aruzzi narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Musa, from Nafi': that Ibn Umar was asked about ghusl on Friday, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded it."
"5661","5652 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition, and our shares reached twelve camels, and we were each given an extra camel."
"5662","5653 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition toward Najd, and their shares reached twelve camels, and they were given, besides that, an extra camel each."
"5663","5654 - And Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn al-Rawwas narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, Burd Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5664","5655 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition among whom was Abdullah ibn Umar, toward Najd, and they gained spoils, and their shares were twelve camels, so they took twelve camels and were given an extra camel each."
"5665","5656 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us on an expedition and they seized much livestock, and we were each given an extra camel. When we returned, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us our shares, and each man among us received twelve camels besides the camel we had been given as extra. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not blame us for what we did, nor for what the one who gave us gave."
"5666","5657 - And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ismail narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: We went on a campaign and gained spoils, and we divided them, and each man among us received twelve camels, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us each an extra camel, so each man among us received thirteen camels."
"5667","5658 - Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Himsi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Zubaydi, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5668","5659 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, who said: The day of Ashura was a day the people of ignorance used to fast. When the fast of Ramadan was made obligatory, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked, and he said: It is a day from the days of Allah; whoever wishes may fast it, and whoever wishes may leave it."
"5669","5660 - Yahya ibn Hakim and Uqbah ibn Mukram al-Ammi narrated to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: They had been commanded to fast Ashura before Ramadan was made obligatory. When Ramadan was made obligatory, whoever wished fasted it and whoever wished left it."
"5670","5661 - And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fasted Ashura and commanded its fasting. When Ramadan was made obligatory, it was left."
"5671","5662 - And Ismail ibn Mas'ud narrated it to us, al-Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he mentioned Ashura to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: It is a day the people of ignorance used to fast; whoever among you wishes, let him fast it, and whoever dislikes, let him leave it."
"5672","5663 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, who said: A surah containing a prostration would be recited in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would prostrate, and we would prostrate, until none of us could find a place for his forehead. And this hadith, we do not know of any isnad for it from Ibn Umar better than this isnad, and none narrated it from Ibn Umar except Nafi'."
"5673","5664 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Abdullah has divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: Order him to take her back until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure. Then if he wishes, let him divorce her before he has intercourse with her, and if he wishes, let him keep her. For that is the waiting period which Allah spoke of."
"5674","5665 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I divorced my wife while she was menstruating, in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Umar ibn al-Khattab asked about that, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Order him to take her back, then keep her until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure. Then if he wishes, let him keep her afterwards, and if he wishes, let him divorce her before he touches her. That is what Allah commanded women to be divorced for."
"5675","5666 - And Sulayman ibn Khallad al-Mu'addib narrated it to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he said: I divorced a wife while she was menstruating, and I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded me to take her back, then keep her until she becomes pure, then menstruates, then becomes pure, then separate from her if it seems fit to me."
"5676","5667 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that he divorced his wife while she was menstruating, and Umar asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who commanded him to take her back, then wait until she menstruates a cycle, then wait until she becomes pure, then divorce her before touching her if he does not wish to keep her. That is the waiting period which Allah commanded women to be divorced for. And when Ibn Umar was asked about a man who divorces his wife while she is menstruating, he would say: Do you know Abdullah ibn Umar? For he divorced his wife while she was menstruating."
"5677","5668 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5678","5669 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-qar' and al-muzaffat."
"5679","5670 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us. 5671 - And Mu'ammal narrated it to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he had finished his sermon, and they said: He forbade al-dubba, al-hantam, and al-muzaffat."
"5680","5672 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari informed me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5681","5673 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, Ubaydullah informed me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."
"5682","5674 - And Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated it to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar. Abdullah ibn Idris said: In the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we used to sleep in the mosque and take our midday rest in it. And Abdullah ibn Numayr said: We used to sleep in the mosque in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5683","5675 - And Ubayd ibn Ismail narrated it to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would go out by the Shajarah road and return by the Mu'arras road."
"5684","5676 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock. The ruler over the people is a shepherd and is responsible for his flock. A man is a shepherd over his household and is responsible for them. A woman is a shepherd over her husband's house and is responsible. A slave is a shepherd over his master's wealth and is responsible for it. So each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible."
"5685","5677 - And Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi narrated it to us, my father narrated to me, Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Asma ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5686","5678 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated it to us, Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Ubaydullah."
"5687","5679 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith: Each of you is a shepherd."
"5688","5680 - And al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub al-Rukhami narrated it to us, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock. And the hadith of Ayyub is like the hadith of Ubaydullah."
"5689","5681 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Each of you is a shepherd, and he mentioned similar wording, except that he said: And a woman is a shepherd over her husband's house and his child, and she is responsible for them. And Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas is Basran; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Qattan and Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated from him. Rawh made an error regarding him, and his hadith from Nafi' is a sound hadith."
"5690","5682 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one of you is invited to a wedding feast, let him accept."
"5691","5683 - And Yahya ibn Abdullah narrated it to us, Bishr ibn al-Mufaddal narrated to us, Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording, except that he said: A wedding feast or a wedding celebration."
"5692","5684 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording. He said: Accept the invitation when you are invited. And Ibn Umar would accept while fasting at a wedding."
"5693","5685 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us. 5686 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Horses have good tied in their forelocks until the Day of Judgment."
"5694","5687 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5695","5688 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qati'i narrated it to us, Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Ubaydullah."
"5696","5689 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a Jewish man and a Jewish woman who had committed adultery, and he ordered that they both be stoned. He said: I saw the man shielding her with himself."
"5697","5690 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5698","5691 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Ubaydullah."
"5699","5692 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Abd al-Karim, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman. And the hadith of Abd al-Karim, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abd al-Karim except al-Thawri."
"5700","5693 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, and Umar ibn Ali narrated it to us, Yahya narrated to us, both of them mentioning from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, forgive those who shave. They said: And those who shorten? He said it three times, and when it was the fourth time, he said: And those who shorten."
"5701","5694 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5702","5695 - Ubayd ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two prostrations before Zuhr and two prostrations after it, and two prostrations after Friday prayer. As for Maghrib, Isha, and Friday, the Prophet prayed them in his house. As for Fajr, it was a time when no one would enter upon him, and Hafsah told me that he would pray it as two light prostrations when dawn broke."
"5703","5696 - Sulayman ibn Khallad al-Mu'addib narrated to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Fulayh ibn Sulayman, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two after it, two before Asr, two after Maghrib, and two after Friday prayer. Nafi' said, from Ibn Umar: And Hafsah informed me that he would pray two light rak'ahs in his house when dawn broke, until I thought he did not recite in them."
"5704","5697 - And Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi narrated it to us, Yahya ibn Salih al-Wuhazi narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And from Hafsah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5705","5698 - Ubayd ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah gathers the first and the last, a banner will be raised for every traitor, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"5706","5699 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5707","5700 - Ubayd ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw him, when his she-camel had settled with him, entering ihram at the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah."
"5708","5701 - Ubayd narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade buying fruits until their ripeness appears; he forbade both the seller and the buyer."
"5709","5702 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording. And he added in it: Until they turn rosy, and crops until they whiten and are safe from blight; he forbade both the seller and the buyer."
"5710","5703 - And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording. And he added in it: Until they turn rosy, and crops until they whiten. And these words, until they whiten, none narrated them except Ayyub."
"5711","5704 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated it to us, Yazid, meaning Ibn Harun, narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Do not trade fruits until their ripeness appears."
"5712","5705 - And Ubayd narrated it to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us. 5706 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Yahya narrated to us, both of them mentioning from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw sputum in the qiblah and scraped it off, then turned to the people and said: When one of you is in prayer, let him not spit in front of his face, for Allah is in front of one's face when he is in prayer."
"5713","5707 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw sputum in the qiblah of the mosque and scraped it off with his hand, then turned to the people and rebuked them angrily, and said: Allah is in front of one's face in his prayer, so let none of you spit in front of his face in his prayer."
"5714","5708 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, al-Dahhak ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he saw sputum in the qiblah of the mosque while he was praying, and after he finished his prayer he said, then he mentioned similar wording."
"5715","5709 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he would order a spear on Eid day, and would go out and pray toward it with the people behind him, and he would do that in travel."
"5716","5710 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Hammad ibn Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar would pray the Eid prayer before the sermon, then deliver the sermon."
"5717","5711 - Sadaqah ibn al-Fadl al-Ammi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dinner is placed and the prayer is established, begin with dinner."
"5718","5712 - And al-Habbari Ubayd ibn Ismail narrated it to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with the same wording. And he added in it: Let him not hasten until he has finished it."
"5719","5713 - And Abu Kamil narrated it to us, Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Abdullah ibn Numayr."
"5720","5714 - Abd al-Wahid ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day: Tell me of a tree that resembles the Muslim, whose leaves do not fall, which gives its fruit at all times by its Lord's permission. It occurred to me that it was the palm tree. He said: The people remained silent, and the Prophet said: It is the palm tree. I said to my father: It had occurred to me that it was the palm tree. He said: What prevented you from saying it to the Messenger of Allah? For you to have said it would be dearer to me than such-and-such. I said: You and Abu Bakr were among the people and you said nothing, so I disliked speaking."
"5721","5715 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Salim ibn Nuh narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No one endures the hardship and severity of Madinah except that I will be a witness or an intercessor for him."
"5722","5716 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Uthman ibn Umar narrated to us, Isa ibn Hafs ibn Asim narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever endures its hardship and severity, I will be an intercessor or a witness for him on the Day of Judgment."
"5723","5717 - Abu al-Sa'ib Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."
"5724","5718 - And Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: There was no story-preaching in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor in the time of Abu Bakr, nor Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except al-Thawri and Abu Usamah."
"5725","5719 - Salm ibn Junadah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: We used to drink in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while walking, and eat while hurrying. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"5726","5720 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abu Khalid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he would pray toward a camel, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray toward his camel. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Abu Khalid and Sharik."
"5727","5721 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Qurashi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you passes by a garden, let him eat, but not take a bundle. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Yahya ibn Sulaym."
"5728","5722 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of wala' and its gifting."
"5729","5723 - And Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated it to us, my father narrated to me, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, and from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of wala' and its gifting. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Yahya ibn Sulaym and Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi. It is only known from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, and Yahya ibn Sa'id combined the two isnads, from Nafi' and from Abdullah ibn Dinar."
"5730","5724 - Abd al-Wahhab ibn al-Hakam al-Warraq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman, and they would pray Zuhr and Asr as two rak'ahs each, praying nothing before or after them. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ubaydullah except through Yahya ibn Sulaym."
"5731","5725 - And al-Hasan ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith retreats to Madinah as a snake retreats to its hole. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Yahya ibn Sulaym. And others narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Khubayb, from Hafs, from Abu Hurayrah, and that is the correct one."
"5732","5726 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to Abu Bakr: When do you pray witr? He said: I pray witr and then sleep. He said: You have taken with firmness. And he said to Umar: When do you pray witr? He said: I sleep, then rise at night and pray witr. He said: You did with strength. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Yahya ibn Sulaym."
"5733","5727 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) burned the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir."
"5734","5728 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated it to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Sufyan, meaning al-Thawri, narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut down the palm trees of Banu al-Nadir and burned them. And the hadith of Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Uqbah ibn Khalid."
"5735","5729 - Yahya ibn Ja'far al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw rain, he would say: Wholesome abundant rain. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Ali ibn Asim. And others narrated it from Ubaydullah, from al-Qasim, from Aishah."
"5736","5730 - Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Bakr and Umar are the masters of the elderly of Paradise among the first and the last, except the prophets and messengers. Do not inform them, O Ali."
"5737","5731 - And Muhammad ibn Hisham narrated it to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi, from Ali. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Abd al-Rahman ibn Malik ibn Mighwal, and we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and Abd al-Rahman is weak in hadith."
"5738","5732 - Hisham ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever enters ihram for Hajj and Umrah, one tawaf suffices him. And this hadith was narrated by al-Darawardi, and Ibn Yaman narrated it from al-Thawri."
"5739","5733 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman stopped at al-Abtah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Abd al-Razzaq."
"5740","5734 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Amr ibn Hashim Abu Malik al-Janbi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that they were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in al-Hijr, and they kneaded dough with water from the well of Thamud and drew water, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that the water be spilled and the dough be fed to the camels, and he said: Draw water from the well of Salih. And this hadith was narrated from Ubaydullah by Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq and Amr ibn Hashim."
"5741","5735 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: There were no more than about twenty white hairs on the head and beard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Sharik, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sharik except Yahya ibn Adam."
"5742","5736 - Abdullah ibn Abi Mawaddah al-Anbari narrated to us, Minjab ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Satan eats with his left and drinks with his left, so let one of you eat with his right and drink with his right. And Sharik erred in this hadith; the reliable narrators only narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr, from his grandfather Ibn Umar, and that is the correct one."
"5743","5737 - Al-Husayn ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, Amr ibn Muhammad al-Anqazi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Idris narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Throne shook for the death of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated with this wording except from Ibn Idris, from Ubaydullah."
"5744","5738 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id al-Kindi narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Yaman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought his sacrificial animals from Qudayd."
"5745","5739 - And Ismail ibn Hafs narrated it to us, Yahya ibn Yaman narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought his sacrificial animals from Qudayd. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except al-Thawri, and none narrated it from al-Thawri except Yahya ibn Yaman."
"5746","5740 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Abu Salamah al-Khuza'i Mansur ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: We used to say: The best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) are Abu Bakr, Umar, and Uthman. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah."
"5747","5741 - Al-Hasan ibn al-Sabbah al-Bazzaz narrated to us, Abu Uthman Sa'id ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The adhan in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was twice, and the iqamah once. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Isa ibn Yunus, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Isa except Sa'id ibn al-Mughirah."
"5748","5742 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-A'la informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that when he entered prayer, he would say takbir and raise his hands, and when he bowed he would raise his hands, and when he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, he would raise his hands. And he raised that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar as musnad except Abd al-A'la. Others narrated it as mawquf, and Ubaydullah narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father. And from Abd al-A'la, both hadiths together: the hadith of Salim as marfu', and the hadith of Nafi' as marfu'."
"5749","5743 - And Nasr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Abd al-A'la informed us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that a woman entered Hell because of a cat she had tied up; she neither fed it nor let it eat from the vermin of the earth. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Abd al-A'la."
"5750","5744 - And al-Husayn ibn Ali ibn Yazid al-Suda'i narrated to us, Hammad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: Aishah and Hafsah woke up fasting, and food was gifted to them, so they broke their fast. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in, and one of them asked him, I think it was Hafsah, and he said: Make up a day in its place. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and Hammad ibn al-Walid is weak in hadith. We only recorded from his hadith what we did not hear from anyone else's hadith, and I think Abdullah narrates this hadith from al-Zuhri, that Aishah and Hafsah, as mursal."
"5751","5745 - Abdullah ibn al-Waddah al-Kufi narrated to us, Amr ibn Hashim al-Janbi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: A woman would borrow jewelry and then keep it, and her matter was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O so-and-so, stand and take her hand and cut it off. And this hadith has no basis from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abd al-Razzaq narrated this hadith: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that a woman in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would borrow goods and deny them, and she was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who ordered that she be cut, and he was interceded with regarding her but refused except to cut her, or words to this effect. And no basis is known for the hadith of Ma'mar from Ayyub from Nafi', nor for the hadith of Ubaydullah from Nafi', from the hadith of Ubaydullah from Nafi' from Ibn Umar. This hadith is among what people criticized Ma'mar for; they said: He narrated a hadith that has no basis, because it contradicts the Book and the Sunnah. And Amr ibn Hashim, his hadith should have been abandoned because of this hadith, and I think he was prompted, and Allah knows best."
"5752","5746 - Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand angels descended on the day Sa'd ibn Mu'adh died, who had never descended before that, and the grave squeezed him. Then Nafi' wept. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Umar, except Dawud al-Attar, and others narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', as mursal."
"5753","5747 - And Sulayman narrated to us, Abu Attab narrated to us, Miskin ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand angels descended for the death of Sa'd ibn Mu'adh; they had never trod the earth before it. And when he was buried, he said: Glory be to Allah, if anyone were to escape the pressure of the grave, Sa'd would have escaped it."
"5754","5748 - And Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted the camel herders to throw at night. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Muslim ibn Khalid, and we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain."
"5755","5749 - Ahmad ibn Aban al-Qurashi narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that an army gained food and honey in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and it was not subjected to khums. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Anas ibn Iyad Abu Damrah."
"5756","5750 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from an expedition and said: O people, do not come to women at night, and do not unsettle them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Muhammad ibn Ubayd. It is only known from the hadith of Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."
"5757","5751 - Muhammad ibn Amir ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hospitality is three days; what exceeds that is charity. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Mubarak ibn Fadalah, and none narrated it from Mubarak except Amir ibn Ibrahim."
"5758","5752 - Ahmad ibn al-Mu'alla al-Adami narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ammar al-Tahi narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am but a servant; I eat as a servant eats. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a connected isnad from him except through this chain, and we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ibn Umar, and none narrated it from Ubaydullah except Mubarak, and none from Mubarak except Hafs ibn Ammar, and he was not corroborated in it."
"5759","5753 - Muhammad ibn al-Mu'ammal ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Hammad narrated to us, Sayf ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever insults my Companions, upon him is the curse of Allah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Sayf."
"5760","5754 - Muhammad ibn Hassan al-Azraq narrated to us, Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Asim ibn Umar narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed Usamah ibn Zayd over an army among whom were Abu Bakr and Umar, and the people criticized his command. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed the people and said: I have heard that you criticized the command of Usamah and the command of his father before him. His father was fit for command, and he is fit for command, meaning Usamah, and he is among the most beloved of people to me, and I commend him to you, I think he said, with good. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Asim ibn Umar. It is only known from the hadith of Musa ibn Uqbah, from Salim, from his father."
"5761","5755 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ma'mar, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he sat in prayer, would place his hands on his knees, raise his right finger next to the thumb and supplicate with it, and place his left hand on his left knee spread upon it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Ma'mar."
"5762","5756 - Nahar ibn Uthman narrated to us, al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of your names are Abdullah and Abd al-Rahman. And this hadith is only preserved from Abdullah ibn Umar, and we have not heard anyone narrate it from al-Mu'tamir, from Ubaydullah, other than Nahar, and he was trustworthy and reliable."
"5763","5757 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hanan narrated to us, Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade al-qazz and silk. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Baqiyyah."
"5764","5758 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, Abu Sa'id al-Taghlibi Muhammad ibn As'ad narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If there is healing in any of your medicines, then it is in a cupper's incision, I think he said, or a sip of honey. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah."
"5765","5759 - Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ifadah on the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and prayed Zuhr at Mina. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Abd al-Razzaq, from Ubaydullah."
"5766","5760 - Salm ibn Junadah ibn Salm narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5767","5761 - And Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, and the wording is Muhammad's, they said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet, peace be upon him."
"5768","5762 - And al-Fadl ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5769","5763 - And Ibrahim ibn Ubaydullah ibn al-Junayd narrated to us, Ibn Abi Maryam narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Uqbah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They are close in their narrations, and the wording is the wording of Musa ibn Uqbah, though the meaning of Abdullah's hadith resembles the meaning of Musa's hadith. He said: While three men were walking, rain overtook them, and they sheltered in a cave in a mountain and entered it. A rock fell over the mouth of their cave and sealed them in. They said to one another: Look to righteous deeds you have done and supplicate Allah with them; perhaps He will open it, or relieve us through them. One of them said: O Allah, I had two elderly aged parents, a wife, and small young children. I would shepherd for them, and when I returned to them I would milk, beginning with my parents, giving them to drink first. One day I was late and did not come until evening, and I found them asleep. I milked as I used to milk, brought the milk, and stood over their heads, disliking to wake them and disliking to begin with the children before them, while the children cried at my feet. That remained my habit and theirs until dawn broke. If You know I did that seeking Your Face, then open for us an opening through which we see the sky. Allah opened an opening in it, and they saw the sky. Another said: O Allah, if You know that I had a cousin whom I loved as a man loves women most intensely, and I sought her for herself but she refused until I bring her one hundred dinars. I strove until I brought one hundred dinars, and I brought them to her. When I sat between her legs, she said: O servant of Allah, fear Allah, and do not break the seal except by its right. So I rose from her. If You know I did that seeking Your Face, then open an opening for them. He opened an opening for them. And the other said: O Allah, if You know that I hired a worker for a faraq of corn, and when he finished his work he said: Give me my due. I offered him his faraq, but he left it and turned away from it. I kept investing it until I gathered from it cattle and their herdsman. He came to me and said: Fear Allah and do not wrong me; give me my due. I said: Go to those cattle and their herdsman. He said: Fear Allah and do not mock me. I said: I am not mocking you; take those cattle and their herdsman. He took them and went with them. If You know I did that seeking Your Face, then open. He relieved them from it, and they left, I think he said, walking. And the hadith of Ubaydullah ibn Umar, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ali ibn Mushir and Junadah ibn Salm."
"5770","5764 - And Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated it to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, my father and Raqabah narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar. And the hadith of Raqabah and Fudayl, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Ibn Fudayl from them."
"5771","5765 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5772","5766 - And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5773","5767 - And Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated it to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And the wording is the wording of Ubaydullah, who said: Whichever date palms are sold with their roots, their fruit belongs to the one who pollinated them, unless the buyer stipulates. And Malik said: Whoever sells pollinated date palms, their fruit belongs to the seller, unless the buyer stipulates."
"5774","5768 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Umar ibn Muhammad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5775","5769 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina two rak'ahs, with Abu Bakr two rak'ahs, with Umar two rak'ahs, and with Uthman two rak'ahs in the early part of his rule, then he completed afterwards."
"5776","5770 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold or silver, placing its stone toward his palm. The people took rings, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) discarded it and said: I will never wear it."
"5777","5771 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring of gold, and he would place its stone toward the inside of his palm. One day he discarded it, and the people discarded their rings. After that he took a ring of silver, and he would seal with it but not wear it."
"5778","5772 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, Abd al-Warith informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5779","5773 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Ziyad al-Mawsili, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wore a ring of gold for three days. When his Companions saw it, gold rings spread among them, so he threw it away, and it is not known what happened to it. He took a ring of silver and ordered that it be engraved: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah. It was in the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he died, in the hand of Abu Bakr until he died, in the hand of Umar until he died, and in the hand of Uthman for years of his rule. When writings increased upon him, he gave it to a man of the Ansar, who would seal with it. The Ansari went out to the well of Uthman, and it fell from him and was never found. He ordered a ring like it, and engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"5780","5774 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) engraved on his ring: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah, and said: Let no one engrave upon my ring."
"5781","5775 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a ring of gold and wore it on his right, with its stone inside. The people wore gold rings. He said: He ascended the pulpit, threw it away, and forbade wearing gold rings."
"5782","5776 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, Nafi' informed me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever keeps a dog, except a hunting dog or a livestock dog, two qirats are deducted from his deed every day."
"5783","5777 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5784","5778 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let not a man make a man leave his seat and then sit in it; rather, make room and widen."
"5785","5779 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man make a man leave his sitting place and then sit in it. I said: On Friday? He said: On Friday and other than it."
"5786","5780 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Amir, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you make a man leave his seat and then sit in it."
"5787","5781 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Rawh narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5788","5782 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Sahl ibn Yusuf narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', who said: Ibn Umar would run three circuits and walk four, mentioning that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"5789","5783 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, Yahya narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5790","5784 - And Sulayman ibn Khallad narrated it to us, Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ran three circuits and walked four, for Hajj and Umrah."
"5791","5785 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, Hammad ibn Mas'adah narrated to us, Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, he, Uthman ibn Talhah, Usamah ibn Zayd, and Bilal. He stayed and lengthened, then came out. I was the first of the people to enter after him, and Bilal was at the House. I asked Bilal: Where did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray? He said: Between the two front pillars."
"5792","5786 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Ibn Abi Adiyy narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5793","5787 - And Bishr ibn Khalid narrated it to us, Sa'id ibn Maslamah informed us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), like the hadith of Ubaydullah."
"5794","5788 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, Yahya ibn Sa'id, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered ihram when his mount stood straight with him."
"5795","5789 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5796","5790 - Ubayd ibn Ismail al-Habbari narrated to us, Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar."
"5797","5791 - And Ubayd ibn Asbat ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn Ismail narrated it to us, they said: Asbat, meaning Ibn Muhammad, narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that Umar vowed to perform i'tikaf for a night in the time of ignorance. When he accepted Islam, he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Fulfill it."
"5798","5792 - Muhammad ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar and Ismail ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tasbih is for men, and clapping is for women."
"5799","5793 - Ziyad ibn Yahya Abu al-Khattab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Maymun al-Makki narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us holding something in his hand. He opened his right hand and said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate: a book from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, containing the people of Paradise with their numbers, names, and lineages, summed against them until the Day of Judgment. None of them is decreased, and none is added among them. The fortunate one may be led on the path of wretchedness until it is said: He is among them, how he resembles them. Then he is moved to his felicity before his death, even by a camel's milking interval. And he opened his left hand and said: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate: a book from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, containing the people of Hell with their numbers, names, and lineages, summed against them until the Day of Judgment. None of them is decreased, and none is added among them. The wretched may be led on the path of the fortunate until it is said: He is among them, how he resembles them. Then his wretchedness overtakes him before his death, even by a camel's milking interval. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are by their endings, deeds are by their endings. Three times. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ubaydullah except Ibn Maymun al-Makki, and he is righteous."
"5800","5794 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, who said, and I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever swears and says: If Allah wills, he has a choice: if he wishes, let him proceed with his oath, and if he wishes to return, there is no harm."
"5801","5795 - And Amr ibn Yahya ibn Ghufrah narrated it to us, he said: Abd al-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever swears an oath and says: If Allah wills, he has not broken his oath. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it in musnad form except Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar. And Ubaydullah narrated it, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, as mawquf, except a man I heard narrating from Abu Muawiyah, from Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I denounced it against him, and he is Abbas al-Bahrani."
"5802","5796 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever drinks wine in this world will not drink it in the Hereafter. And this hadith was narrated by others besides Shu'bah, and we only mentioned it from Shu'bah because of how little Shu'bah narrated in musnad form from Ayyub."
"5803","5797 - And Sulayman ibn Ubaydullah al-Ghaylani narrated to us, he said: Abu Qutaybah narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What clothes may the muhrim wear? He said: He must not wear the shirt, nor trousers, nor leather socks, unless he cannot find sandals, nor any garment touched by saffron or wars. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Abu Qutaybah. And it was narrated from Ayyub by more than one."
"5804","5798 - Abu Musa narrated it to us, from Abd al-Wahhab. 5799 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Jews brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two Jews who had committed adultery, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What do you find in your Book? They said: They are flogged. He said: You have lied, indeed stoning is in it, so bring the Torah and recite it if you are truthful. Ibn Salam said: We find stoning in it, so they brought the Torah. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring me a man from among you. So they brought him a young one-eyed man called Ibn Suriya, and he said: Are you the most knowledgeable of them? He said: They do say that, he said: Then recite. So he recited until he came to the place of stoning, then he placed his hand over it, meaning the verse of stoning, so he said: Lift your hand. The Jew said: O Muhammad, indeed stoning is in it, he said: So he ordered that they both be stoned. Ibn Umar said: It is as if I see him shielding her from the stones with himself."
"5805","5800 - And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated it to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it. And this hadith was narrated by Ubaydullah in abridged form, and Ayyub added in it, so we repeated it because of the addition, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah, from Ayyub, except Yazid ibn Zuray."
"5806","5801 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Asim ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it, or close to it."
"5807","5802 - Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When you are three, then two must not converse privately excluding their companion. And he forbade that a man make a man get up from his seat and then sit in it."
"5808","5803 - And Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated it to us, he said: Isma'il narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"5809","5804 - Ahmad ibn Abdullah ibn Ali ibn Suwayd ibn Manjuf narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The two sellers have the choice so long as they have not separated. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah, from Ayyub, except Sa'id ibn Amir, and it is only preserved from the hadith of Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, from Ayyub. And I fear that Sa'id ibn Amir erred in it."
"5810","5805 - And Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"5811","5806 - Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Do not prevent your women from the mosques."
"5812","5807 - And with this isnad: When one of you goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe."
"5813","5808 - And with this isnad: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whenever a man sells date-palms that have been pollinated, their fruit belongs to the seller unless the buyer stipulates otherwise. And these hadiths were narrated by a group from Ayyub, and from others besides Ayyub, but we repeated them only because of Shu'bah from Ayyub."
"5814","5809 - Al-Husayn ibn Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Muslim narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade travelling with the Quran to the land of the enemy. And this hadith was narrated by a group from Ayyub, among them Hammad ibn Zayd and Ibn Ulayyah and others, but we do not know anyone who narrated it from Shu'bah except Muslim."
"5815","5810 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not ... the mosques, and let them go out ... [text truncated in source]."
"5816","(Text effaced in print; no matn preserved.)"
"5817","(Text effaced in print; no matn preserved.)"
"5818","5813 - Mu'ammal narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from a Hajj or Umrah and ascended a high mound of earth - or he said: an elevation - he said: Allah is Greatest, Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, there is no god but Allah alone with no partner for Him, to Him belongs sovereignty and to Him belongs praise and He is over all things Capable, returning, repenting, to our Lord praising, Allah spoke His promise truly and aided His servant and defeated the confederates alone."
"5819","5814 - Amr ibn Ali and Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw as if in my hand there was a piece of silk brocade, and wherever I aimed it at a place it flew with me to it, so Hafsah narrated it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Indeed your brother is a righteous man. Or: Indeed Abdullah is a righteous man. And this hadith we do not preserve with this wording except from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."
"5820","5815 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, they said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: People used to see dreams and narrate them to the Messenger of Allah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I see your dreams have concurred upon the last seven, so whoever among you seeks it, let him seek it in the last seven."
"5821","5816 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade muzabanah. He said: And Nafi used to explain it saying: Fruit bought by its estimate in dates and a named measure; if it increases it is for you, and if it decreases it is upon you."
"5822","5817 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that the fruit of date-palms be sold until it reddens, and ears of grain and crops until they whiten and are safe from blight. He forbade the seller and the buyer."
"5823","5818 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it. This is sahih; Ibn Ulayyah also narrated it in musnad form, and it is the hadith of Ayyub."
"5824","5819 - Abu Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Your likeness and the likeness of the Jews and Christians is like a man who employed workers and said: Who will work for me from morning until midday for a qirat? So the Jews worked, then he said: Who will work for me from midday until Asr prayer for a qirat? So the Christians worked from midday until Asr prayer, then he said: Who will work for me from Asr prayer until Maghrib for two qirats? So you worked, so the Jews and Christians became angry and said: We worked more and were paid less?! He said: Did I wrong you anything? They said: No, he said: That is My bounty, I give it to whom I will."
"5825","5820 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn al-Akhnas narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Your lifespans compared to the lifespans of those who passed are like what is between Asr prayer until sunset, and your likeness and the likeness of the Jews and Christians is like a man who employed workers. Then he mentioned similar to it."
"5826","5821 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, from where do you command us to enter ihram? He said: The people of Madinah enter ihram from Dhu al-Hulayfah, and the people of Sham from al-Juhfah, and the people of Najd from Qarn. He said: And they say: And the people of Yemen from Yalamlam."
"5827","5822 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that he was urgently summoned regarding Safiyyah, so he travelled in one night the distance of three nights, he travelled until evening came, so I said to him: The prayer, but he did not turn and travelled until it grew dark, so a man said: The prayer, evening has come, so he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when travel pressed him used to join these two prayers, and I want to join them, so he travelled until the twilight disappeared, then alighted and joined them."
"5828","5823 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) two rakahs before Zuhr and two after it, and two after Maghrib in his house, and two after Isha. And Hafsah narrated to me: that he used to pray after dawn rose and the caller called to prayer two light rakahs, and it was an hour in which no one entered upon him."
"5829","5824 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbuwayh narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Muawiyah ibn Sallam narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"5830","5825 - Sawwar ibn Sahl al-Duba'i narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When you lay your dead in the grave, say: In the name of Allah and upon the sunnah of the Messenger of Allah."
"5831","5826 - And Sawwar narrated it to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Amir narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Siddiq, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it. And the hadith of Ayyub, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah except Sa'id ibn Amir."
"5832","5827 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to mourn over a dead person for more than three days, except a woman over her husband, for she mourns over him four months and ten days. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Hammad ibn Salamah, and others narrate from Nafi, from Safiyyah, from one of the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5833","5828 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: al-Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed in Jahiliyyah to observe itikaf for a day in the Sacred Mosque, he said: Go and fulfil your vow. And with him was a boy from the captives of Hawazin, and he heard people saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has freed the captives of Hawazin, so he said: Go, for you are free."
"5834","5829 - And Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated it to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar ... with similar to it, or close to it."
"5835","5830 - Al-Husayn ibn Mahdi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shaved in his Hajj. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Ma'mar."
"5836","5831 - And Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Ibrahim ibn Ishkab narrated it to us, he said: Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"5837","5832 - Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Mukharrimi narrated to us, he said: Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray on the khumrah. I think he said: And he used to pray and prostrate upon it."
"5838","5833 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id al-Jawhari narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ayyub, and Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said regarding the two handfuls: These are for this, and these are for this. He said: So people dispersed while not disputing about qadar. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from al-Thawri except Abu Ahmad, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Abu Ahmad except Ibrahim ibn Sa'id, and it is not known from Ayyub, nor from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, except through this channel."
"5839","5834 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah, meaning Ibn Musa, narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered his caller on a rainy night of wind and cold while travelling: Pray in your dwellings."
"5840","5835 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, he said: Abu Sadaqah Bakr ibn Sadaqah al-Juddi narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"5841","5836 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Qays al-Raqashi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man from the people of Paradise will enter upon you. Then Sa'd entered, he said that on three days, each time Sa'd entered. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Abdullah ibn Qays, and he heard it only from Abu Musa from him."
"5842","5837 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, he said: Ibn Umar heard a man saying: O son of the disciple of the Messenger of Allah, he said: If you are from the family of al-Zubayr, otherwise not. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah, and from Sa'id except Yazid ibn Harun."
"5843","5838 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever sees an afflicted person and says: Praise be to Allah who spared me from what He tried you with and preferred me over many of His creation with preference - that affliction will never befall him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, and al-Mughirah is unobjectionable, a well-known Basran, and the hadith is gharib."
"5844","5839 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Jahm narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade jallalah animals and riding upon them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"5845","5840 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Shayban ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Surayj narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to withhold seeking forgiveness for the people of major sins until we heard our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah does not forgive that partners be associated with Him, and He forgives what is less than that for whom He wills, and he said: I have deferred my intercession for the people of major sins of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection. And these words we do not know to be narrated from Ibn Umar except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ayyub except Harb ibn Surayj, and he is a man from Basra, unobjectionable."
"5846","5841 - Yahya ibn Ward ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Ayyub narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed Allah is Witr and loves witr."
"5847","5842 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Mu'adh ibn Hisham narrated to us, from his father, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever among you is able to die in Madinah, let him die there, for I intercede for whoever dies in it."
"5848","5843 - Amr ibn Ali and Yahya ibn Hakim and Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, they said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to pray witr upon his mount."
"5849","5844 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the burnus, meaning for the muhrim."
"5850","5845 - And Yahya ibn Habib ibn Arabi narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, he said: Ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate against four, so there was revealed: Not for you is the decision whether He turns to them or punishes them, for indeed they are wrongdoers."
"5851","5846 - And al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a noble man of a people comes to you, honour him."
"5852","5847 - And Khalid ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When we missed a man at Isha and Fajr, we thought ill of him."
"5853","5848 - And Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated it to us, he said: Abu Khalid Sulayman ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When we missed a man from Fajr prayer, we thought ill of him."
"5854","5849 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he used to breathe in the vessel three times."
"5855","5850 - Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr narrated to us, he said: Ubays ibn Marhum narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When they are three, then two must not converse privately excluding the third, and when they are three on a journey, let one of them lead them."
"5856","5851 - And one of our companions narrated to us, from Khalid ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not come to women at night. And these hadiths we mentioned from Ibn Ajlan because we do not know anyone who corroborated Ibn Ajlan in them from the hadith of Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except the hadith: Do not come to women at night, and the beginning of the hadith: When they are three, two must not converse privately excluding the third, for these two were narrated by others besides Ibn Ajlan, and the rest we do not know anyone who narrated them except Ibn Ajlan."
"5857","5852 - Bishr ibn Khalid al-Askari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out one day leaning upon Abu Bakr and Umar, and said: Thus shall we be raised on the Day of Resurrection. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it except Sa'id ibn Maslamah, from Isma'il, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, and he was not corroborated in it."
"5858","5853 - Amr ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sulaym narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited Surah al-Rahman to his companions, and they fell silent, so he said: The jinn were better in response than you; whenever I recited to them: So which of the favours of your Lord will you both deny, they said: We deny nothing of Your favours, our Lord, so to You belongs praise. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this channel with this isnad."
"5859","5854 - And Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq informed us, he said: Ma'mar informed us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man lean upon his hands in prayer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Isma'il ibn Umayyah except Ma'mar."
"5860","5855 - Khalaf ibn Khalifah narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Umayyah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever waits for it until it is buried has two qirats. And this hadith was narrated by al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Ibn Umar. And Salim al-Barrad narrated it, from Ibn Umar."
"5861","5856 - Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Sa'd ibn Ubadah as a collector and said: O Sa'd, beware lest you come on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel that bellows. He said: I will not take it, excuse me, so he excused him. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi."
"5862","5857 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abdullah, meaning Ibn Abi Uways, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ansari narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the shade of the Ka'bah sitting with his arms around his knees."
"5863","5858 - And Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from his brother, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, and Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is unlawful."
"5864","5859 - Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats from this foul tree, or foul greens, let him not approach our prayer place. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari with this isnad except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"5865","5860 - Al-Hasan ibn Yazid ibn Abi Yazid Abu Ali al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Ismah ibn Muhammad al-Ansari narrated to us, of the descendants of Fadalah ibn Ubayd, from Yahya, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar ... [matn missing in source; text breaks off]."
"5866","5861 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Abu Amir narrated to us, he said: Kharijah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Indeed Allah has placed truth upon the heart and tongue of Umar. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Ismah ibn Muhammad, and he was a man not strong in hadith. And Kharijah ibn Abdullah narrated it from Nafi, and Nafi ibn Abi Nu'aym."
"5867","5862 - Al-Hasan ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Ismah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: O Allah, honour Islam through the more beloved of these two men to You; through Umar ibn al-Khattab, or through Abu Jahl ibn Hisham. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Ismah, and we have already mentioned Ismah. And others besides Kharijah narrated it, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."
"5868","5863 - Abdullah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id. 5863 (m) - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated it to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us. Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I have acquired land at Khaybar - and Ibn Awn said in his hadith: I acquired wealth at Khaybar - no wealth I have acquired is more precious to me than it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, give its produce in charity and keep its principal, so he gave it in charity, not to be sold, nor given away, nor inherited, and he placed it for the poor, and the wayfarer, and slaves, and relatives, and the guest; there is no sin upon whoever administers it to eat from it in a proper manner, without hoarding from it. And this wording is the wording of Ibn Awn, and Ibn Ulayyah said in his hadith: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Keep its principal and give its produce in charity. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it except Ibn Awn, and he is known by it, and as for the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id, it was only narrated by Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib from him."
"5869","5864 - Nasr ibn Ali, and Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us, and the wording is Nasr's, he said: Yazid ibn Harun informed us: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari informed us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that a slave girl of the family of Ka'b used to graze sheep, and she feared that one of them would die, so she took a stone and slaughtered it with it, and she mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered that it be eaten."
"5870","5865 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated it to us, he said: Marhum ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, he said: Dawud, meaning Ibn Abd al-Rahman, narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah. 5866 - And Ayyub ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mushir narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to the hadith of Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Yazid ibn Harun and Ibn Numayr, and people only narrate it from Yahya, from Nafi, in mursal form. And we do not know anyone who narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah except Dawud ibn Abd al-Rahman, and he is weak. And the hadith is only narrated by Ubaydullah and al-Hajjaj, from Nafi, from Ibn Ka'b ibn Malik, from his father. And that is correct."
"5871","5867 - Yahya ibn al-Mu'alla ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to say in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman, then we did not prefer any of his companions over another."
"5872","5868 - Rawh ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Harb narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar said to people who visit the ruler: What wrong that you saw from him did you change, or what good did you command him with? They said: No, but when he says something we say: He spoke the truth, and when we leave him we say: We do not know. He said: We used to count this as hypocrisy, or part of hypocrisy. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi, except Hammad ibn Zayd, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Hammad ibn Zayd except Sulayman ibn Harb."
"5873","5869 - Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) separated the two who invoke curses, and attached the child to its mother. And this wording we do not know anyone who narrated it except Malik, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."
"5874","5870 - And Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Makki ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi."
"5875","5871 - And Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he prayed over al-Najashi and said takbir over him four times. And the hadith of Malik, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Malik except Makki ibn Ibrahim, from Malik. And the hadith of Fulayh, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Fulayh except al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan."
"5876","5872 - And Muhammad ibn Ammar al-Razi narrated it to us, he said: Makki narrated to us, he said: Malik, and Abdullah ibn Ziyad ibn Sam'an narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar ... Abu Bakr said: And I think Makki carried the hadith of Abdullah ibn Sam'an, from Nafi, onto the hadith of Malik, so it became confused to him."
"5877","5873 - Muhammad ibn Yahya, and Hatim ibn Bakr narrated to us, they said: Bishr ibn Umar narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he was asked about the fear prayer, so he said: The imam advances with a group of people and prays with them one rakah, while another group stays between him and the enemy having not prayed, then when those with him have prayed one rakah, those others come and he prays with them one rakah, then he gives salam, and each of the two groups stands and prays one rakah. And I think he raised that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith in musnad form except Malik."
"5878","5874 - And Umar ibn al-Khattab and al-Abbas ibn Abdullah narrated it to us, they said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with one of the two groups one rakah and two prostrations, while the other group faced the enemy, then the group that was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left and the other group came, so he prayed with them one rakah and two prostrations, then gave salam, and each of the two groups stood and prayed for itself one rakah and two prostrations. And this hadith is gharib from Ayyub ibn Musa, and it is not with Ubaydullah."
"5879","5875 - Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, he said: Atiq ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of gharar."
"5880","5876 - Umayr ibn Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Nafi ibn Thabit al-Zubayri narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer eats in one intestine, and the disbeliever eats in seven intestines. Abdullah ibn Nafi ibn Thabit al-Zubayri is a Madinan, trustworthy, and he is not Abdullah ibn Nafi al-Sa'igh."
"5881","5877 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Malik narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that A'ishah wanted to buy a slave girl and free her, so her people said: We sell her on condition that her wala is for us, so she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That must not prevent you, for wala belongs only to whoever frees."
"5882","5878 - And Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that A'ishah bargained for Barirah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned from prayer, so she said: They refused to sell her unless they stipulate the wala, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wala belongs to whoever frees."
"5883","5879 - Bishr ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: Abu Usamah narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to the house of his daughter Fatimah, then returned and did not enter, so Ali came, and she mentioned that to him, so he mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: I saw a curtain over her door. So Ali mentioned that to Fatimah, and she said: Then command me as you wish, so Ali mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Send it to the sons of so-and-so, for they need it. And this wording we do not know anyone who narrated it except Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Nafi."
"5884","5880 - Bishr ibn Adam narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ata narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... [matn missing in source; text breaks off]."
"5885","5881 - And Bishr ibn Adam narrated it to us, he said: My grandfather Azhar ibn Sa'd narrated to me, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham, they said: O Messenger of Allah, and our Yemen, he said: O Allah, bless for us our Sham, they said: O Messenger of Allah, and our Iraq, he said: There are earthquakes and tribulations, and there - or he said: from it - rises the horn of Satan."
"5886","5882 - Sulayman ibn Khallad al-Mu'addib narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever throws the jamrah with seven pebbles, the jamrah at al-Aqabah, then leaves and slaughters a hady, then shaves or shortens, then what was forbidden to him of the rites of Hajj has become lawful for him."
"5887","5883 - And Sulayman ibn Khallad narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastened in three circuits, and walked four, for Hajj and Umrah."
"5888","5884 - And Sulayman ibn Khallad narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Fulayh narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out for Umrah, but the disbelievers of Quraysh came between him and the House, so he slaughtered his hady and shaved his head at al-Hudaybiyah on condition that he perform Umrah the next year, and I think he said: and not enter upon them except with sheathed swords, so he performed Umrah the next year and entered it as before, then when he had stayed three days he left."
"5889","5885 - And Salamah narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan narrated to us, he said: Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man becomes bankrupt and a man finds his property with him - meaning with the bankrupt - intact, he is more entitled to it."
"5890","5886 - Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Dawud al-Sawwaq narrated to us, he said: Ghalib ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Mansur narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out from al-Baqi, Baqi al-Gharqad, and said: Peace upon the people of the abodes of Muslims and believers, and may Allah have mercy on those who went before, and we, if Allah wills, shall join you. And we do not know Abbad ibn Mansur to have narrated in musnad form, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, other than this hadith, and none narrated it from him except this Ghalib."
"5891","5887 - Al-Hasan ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Jarawi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yahya al-Ma'afiri narrated to us, he said: Haywah narrated to us, from Ishaq Abu Abd al-Rahman, that Ata al-Khurasani narrated to him: that Nafi, the freedman of Ibn Umar, narrated to him, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When you trade in inah and take hold of the tails of cows and abandon jihad - Allah will impose upon you a humiliation He will not remove until you return to your religion. And we do not know Ata al-Khurasani to have narrated in musnad form from Nafi other than this hadith, and Ishaq, in my view, is Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah, and he is lenient in hadith."
"5892","5888 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh al-Aqadi narrated to us, he said: Thabit ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to us, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling meat for animals. And this wording we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Thabit, and Thabit is a man from Basra."
"5893","5889 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Durust ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Tariq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, in marfu form, he said: Whoever comes to food to which he was not invited enters as a thief and eats unlawful. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ibn Umar except through this channel, and Aban ibn Tariq, we do not know him to have narrated in musnad form from Nafi other than this hadith, and none narrated it from him except Durust, and Durust is from Basra, there was nothing wrong with him."
"5894","5890 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn al-Rabi al-Yuhmadi narrated to us, from al-Hadrami, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to Allah."
"5895","5891 - Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, they said: Abu Bakr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered from the campaign of Uhud, he heard the women of the Ansar weeping, so he said: But Hamzah has no weepers for him. That reached the Ansar, so their women came and wept over him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood when he heard their voices, he said: Woe to them, they have continued weeping still, order them to return to their homes, and let them not weep over one who perishes after today. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi with this wording except Usamah ibn Zayd."
"5896","5892 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, from Usamah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"5897","5893 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Isa al-Hannat, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in his privy facing the qiblah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Isa."
"5898","5894 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Isra'il, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We remained waiting for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until a third of the night had gone, so he said: There is no one of these religions waiting for prayer besides you; were it not that I would burden my ummah, I would have ordered them to pray at this hour."
"5899","5895 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ... [matn missing in source; text breaks off]."
"5900","5896 - And Sulayman ibn Sayf narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn al-Harith informed us, from Mansur, from al-Hakam, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to the hadith of Isra'il."
"5901","5897 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not ride the sea except as a pilgrim or a warrior. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Layth, and from Layth except Abu Hafs al-Abbar."
"5902","5898 - Yusuf ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Jarir narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Islam began strange and will return as it began, so glad tidings to the strangers. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Layth except Jarir."
"5903","5899 - Abdullah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: al-Muharibi Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no sadaqah in less than five awsuq, and no sadaqah in five awaq."
"5904","5900 - And Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Shayban, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There is no sadaqah in less than five camels ... Then he mentioned similar to it."
"5905","5901 - Al-Fadl ibn Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: The king and the slave, and the husband and the wife, shall be brought, then the king and the slave shall be reckoned, and the husband and the wife, until it is said to the man: You drank on such-and-such day for pleasure, and it is said to the husband: You proposed to so-and-so along with suitors, so I married her to you and left them. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Layth except Sa'id ibn Maslamah."
"5906","5902 - Bishr ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Either from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or from Umar ... [matn missing in source; text breaks off]."
"5907","5903 - And Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Either from the Messenger of Allah, or from Umar. He said: When one of you prays, let him wear his two garments, for Allah is most deserving of being adorned for. And Fudayl added, from Musa, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: If one of you does not have two garments, let him pray in one garment, and let none of you wrap himself in his prayer as the Jews wrap."
"5908","5904 - Al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Za'farani narrated to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Umar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spittle shall be raised on the Day of Resurrection in the qiblah, upon the face of its owner. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."
"5909","5905 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abis narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw spittle in the qiblah of the mosque, so he scraped it, then said: When one of you stands in prayer, let him not spit in front of him, nor to his right, but to his left."
"5910","5906 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: We used to count for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a single sitting a hundred times, saying: My Lord, forgive me and turn to me, indeed You are the Oft-Returning, the Forgiving."
"5911","5907 - And Amr ibn Ali narrated it to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it."
"5912","5908 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar ... [matn missing in source; text breaks off]."
"5913","5909 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad al-Huna'i narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that he used to come to a tree between Makkah and Madinah, rest in its shade at midday, and report that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do that."
"5914","5910 - Abd al-A'la ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar ... [matn missing in source; text breaks off]."
"5915","5911 - And Yahya ibn Ward ibn Abdullah narrated it to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Adi ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Umayyah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the sun eclipsed for the death of a great man among the great, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out and prayed with the people, prolonging the standing until it was said he would not bow from the length of standing, then he bowed until it was said he would not rise from the length of bowing, then he rose and prolonged the standing like his first standing, then he bowed prolonging the bowing like his first bowing, then he raised his head and prostrated, then he did in the other rakah like that, so they were four bowings and four prostrations, then he turned to the people and said: O people, the sun and moon do not eclipse for the death of anyone, nor for his life, but they are two signs among the signs of Allah, so when you see them, hasten to prayer."
"5916","5912 - Abu Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hasan Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Habib al-Raqqi informed us, he said: Ahmad ibn Amr ibn Abd al-Khaliq narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Nafi narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever frees a share, or a portion, or a partnership he owns in a slave, and he has wealth reaching its price at a just valuation, then he is freed from his wealth. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from Yunus except al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman."
"5917","5913 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus, meaning Ibn Ubayd, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two sales in one sale, and said: Delay by the rich is injustice, and when one of you is referred to one who is solvent, let him accept the transfer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Yunus, and none narrated it from Yunus except Hushaym."
"5918","5914 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Ibn Awn narrated to us that he wrote to Nafi asking him about supplication before fighting, so he wrote to him: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raided Banu al-Mustaliq while they were heedless and secure, their cattle being watered at the water, so he killed their fighters and took their offspring captive, and on that day he took Juwayriyah bint al-Harith. Abdullah ibn Umar narrated that to me, and he was in that army. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we do not know it to be narrated from Ibn Umar except from the hadith of Ibn Awn, from Nafi."
"5919","5915 - Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of the believer is like the date-palm. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Ibn Awn except Azhar, and we did not hear anyone narrating it from Azhar except Muhammad ibn Sudran."
"5920","5916 - Abu Bakr ibn Khallad narrated to us, he said: Azhar narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: He commanded us to undo our provision bags after three, meaning of sacrificial meat. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Ibn Awn, and similar to his words was narrated with other wording through various channels from Ibn Umar."
"5921","5917 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Abu Ahmad narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Zayd, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar, when he prayed, would point with his finger and follow it with his gaze, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is harder upon Satan than iron. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Kathir ibn Zayd, and we do not know Kathir ibn Zayd to have narrated in musnad form from Nafi except this hadith."
"5922","5918 - Ibrahim ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Nafi, that Ibn Umar used to perform wudu with his sandals on his feet and wipe over them, and say: Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Ibn Abi Dhi'b, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from him except Rawh, and he only wiped over them because he performed wudu without ritual impurity, and he used to perform wudu for every prayer without impurity; this is its meaning in our view."
"5923","5919 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Rawwad, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that a man from the Ansar saw in a dream, and it was said to him: By what did your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command you? He said: He commanded us to glorify thirty-three times, and to magnify thirty-four times, and to praise thirty-three times, so he said: A hundred times, so he said: Glorify twenty-five times, and praise twenty-five times, and magnify twenty-five times, and declare oneness twenty-five times, so that is a hundred. So he mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Do as the Ansari said. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ibn Umar except through this channel, and we do not know Ali ibn Fudayl ibn Iyad to have narrated in musnad form any hadith other than this hadith."
"5924","5920 - Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, of the descendants of al-Nu'man ibn Bashir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to touch his beard in prayer without fidgeting. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) connected from him except from Ibn Umar from him, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except this Isa ibn Abdullah."
"5925","5921 - Salamah ibn Shabib narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Ayyub narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn al-Had, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Fire is an enemy, so beware of it. He said: And Ibn Umar used to go around the dwelling of his family putting it out. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Ibn Umar through this channel, and Yazid ibn al-Had did not narrate in musnad form from Nafi other than this hadith."
"5926","5922 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl narrated to us, he said: Hammad narrated to us, from Layth, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are those softest in shoulders in prayer. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Layth."
"5927","5923 - Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Jews of Banu al-Nadir and Qurayzah fought the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he expelled Banu al-Nadir and left Qurayzah until Qurayzah fought after that, so he killed their men and divided their women, wealth and children among the Muslims. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Musa ibn Uqbah."
"5928","5924 - Isma'il ibn Mas'ud narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ordered zakat al-fitr on the day of Fitr to be brought out before prayer. And this wording we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Musa ibn Uqbah, and more than one narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah."
"5929","5925 - Al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Neither the junub nor the menstruating woman recites anything of the Quran. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah except Isma'il ibn Ayyash, and we do not know it to be narrated from Ibn Umar through any channel except this channel, and it is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) regarding the menstruating woman except through this channel."
"5930","5926 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: You have seen us, and a Muslim man is no more entitled to his dinar and dirham than his Muslim brother."
"5931","5927 - And Sadaqah ibn al-Fadl narrated it to us, he said: Abu Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar ... with similar to it. And we do not know anyone who narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Mu'awiyah."
"5932","5928 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awn al-Khurasani narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) faced the Stone, touched it, then placed his lips upon it weeping long, then turned and there was Umar weeping, so he said: O Umar, here tears are shed. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated from Ibn Umar except through this channel, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Muhammad ibn Awn. And Muhammad ibn Awn narrated in musnad form, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, two hadiths, this is one of them. And the other: Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated it to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awn narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."
"5933","5929 - And Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated it to us, he said: Shababab ibn Sawwar narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar. Al-Mughirah said, from Ali ibn Thabit also, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: Prayer on a journey is two rakahs; whoever opposes the sunnah has disbelieved."
"5934","5930 - Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Shababab narrated to us, from al-Mughirah ibn Muslim, from Matar al-Warraq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered favour upon the disbelievers, so the free are more entitled, meaning manumission. And this hadith we do not know to be narrated with this wording except from Ibn Umar, and we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Matar, and from Matar except Mughirah ibn Muslim."
"5935","5931 - Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Khallad narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Burd ibn Sinan narrated to us, from his father, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade drinking in vessels of gold and silver."
"5936","5932 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated it to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mahan narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn A'yan narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar to it. And this hadith is only narrated by the huffaz, from Nafi, from Zayd ibn Abdullah, from Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Umm Salamah. And we do not know anyone who said: from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, except Khusayf and Burd."
"5937","5933 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever calls adhan for twelve years, Paradise becomes due for him, and sixty good deeds are written for him for his adhan each time, and thirty good deeds for each iqamah. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it except Abdullah ibn Salih, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."
"5938","5934 - Al-Hasan ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that a man have another man stand up for him in his seat, and when he returns he is more entitled to it. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it from Nafi except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, except something in which, in my view, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab erred, so he narrated it from Abu Shihab, from Abu Ishaq, whereas he meant Ibn Ishaq."
"5939","5935 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'la ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding women in ihram from gloves and face veils, and garments touched by wars and saffron. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrated it with this wording except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar."
"5940","5936 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, he said: Ya'la narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you dozes in his seat on Friday, let him move to another. And these words we do not know to be narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by Ibn Umar, and we know it only from the narration of Ibn Ishaq alone."
"5941","5937 - Ibrahim ibn Hani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, he said: Abu Shihab narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade two conversing privately excluding the third when they are together, and that a man make a man get up from his place and return to it, and when a man returns to his place he is more entitled to it, and when he dozes on Friday let him move from his place. And these hadiths which Abu Shihab narrated, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, are in my view from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, and he erred in them in my view; because the hadith: When he dozes, and: When he stands from his place - none narrated them except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi."
"5942","5938 - Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriyah al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Nafi informed me, from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the heat of fever is from the blast of Hell, so extinguish it with water. He said: And Ibn Umar used to say: O Allah, remove defilement from us."
"5943","5939 - Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: I saw those who buy food in bulk being beaten in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until they returned it to their dwellings. And this hadith, there is disagreement about it from al-Awza'i: some of al-Awza'i's companions narrated it from Nafi, as Abbad narrated it, and Ibn Abi Razin narrated it, from al-Awza'i, from al-Zuhri, from Hamzah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar, from his father. And we do not know anyone who narrated these words from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Umar, and Nafi and Salim narrated it from him."
"5944","5940 - Ibrahim ibn Yusuf al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar ... [matn missing in source; text breaks off]."
"5945","5941 - And Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, he said: Nafi narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Umar: that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to the prayer ground for Adha or Fitr, he ordered a spear to be brought out before him until it was planted in the prayer ground, and it was open space with nothing before him screening him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray towards it."
"5946","5942 - Hawtharah ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Abbad ibn Juwayriyah informed us, al-Awza'i informed us, Nafi' narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting goods before they are brought down to the markets, and he forbade najsh (false bidding to raise price)."
"5947","5943 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi Abd al-Kabir ibn Abd al-Majid informed us, Usamah ibn Zayd informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to slaughter at the musalla (place of prayer)."
"5948","5944 - Yahya ibn al-Sari narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Hajjaj, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained in Medina for such-and-such time, never omitting the sacrifice (udhiya)."
"5949","5945 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Muqaddami narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the people of al-Awali used to perform Friday prayer with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5950","5946 - Ahmad ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Muhammad informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: While a man was looking at his sides (his garments) and was impressed with himself, the earth swallowed him and he keeps sinking in it until the Day of Resurrection."
"5951","5947 - Hilal ibn Bishr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: For whatever the sky waters, the tenth (ushr) is due, and whatever is irrigated by water-wheels, half the tenth is due."
"5952","5948 - Abu Kurayb narrated to us, Mu'awiyah ibn Hisham informed us, Sufyan informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of gharar (uncertainty/risk)."
"5953","5949 - And al-Hasan ibn Muhammad al-Baghdadi informed us of it, Qabisah informed us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5954","5950 - Isma'il ibn Hafs narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Ibrahim ibn Qu'ays, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out while in the mosque there were nine persons: four freedmen and five Arabs, and he said: There will be rulers over you; whoever aids them in their wrongdoing, believes their lies, and frequents their doors, is not from me and I am not from him, and he will never come to me at the Hawd (Pool); and whoever does not aid them in their wrongdoing and does not believe their lies, is from me and I am from him, and he will come to me at the Hawd."
"5955","5951 - al-Hasan ibn Yahya narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sinan informed us, from Abdullah ibn Umar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade that the fortresses (utum) of Medina be demolished."
"5956","5952 - al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, Abu Qutaybah informed us, Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Yazid ibn Umayyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bid farewell to a man, he would take his hand and not let go of his hand until the man was the one to let go of the Prophet's (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hand, and he would say: I entrust to Allah your religion, your trust, and the outcomes of your deeds."
"5957","5953 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Asim informed us, Haywah informed us, from Humayd ibn Sakhr, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be in my ummah swallowing by the earth, transformation, and pelting; and that will be among the people of qadar (deniers of divine decree). And we do not know Yazid ibn Umayyah nor Humayd ibn Sakhr narrated from Nafi' except this hadith which we mentioned from him."
"5958","5954 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, Kawthar ibn Hakim narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ibn Umm Abd, do you know what is Allah's ruling concerning those of this ummah who rebel? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Their wounded are not to be finished off, their captives are not to be killed, their fugitives are not to be pursued, and their fay (spoils) is not to be distributed. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route, nor do we know anyone narrated it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except Ibn Umar, nor do we know anyone narrated it from Nafi' except Kawthar ibn Hakim."
"5959","5955 - Ahmad ibn Malik al-Qushayri narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la informed us, Nafi' informed us, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the sale of habal al-habalah (the unborn offspring of an unborn camel) until it is born then gives birth, he forbade that, and he forbade the sale of an animal for an animal on credit."
"5960","5956 - Ahmad ibn Malik narrated to us, Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The False Messiah, the Dajjal, is blind in the right eye, as if his eye is a floating grape. And Abu Umayyah ibn Ya'la is a man from Basra who is not strong in hadith, though the early scholars narrated from him."
"5961","5957 - And Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abu Bakr al-Hanafi informed us, Abdullah ibn Nafi' informed us, from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: There was a man in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who was cheated in his sales, and he complained about that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he had a speech impediment in his tongue, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you sell, say: No deceit (la khilabah), and when you buy, say: No deceit."
"5962","5958 - And Yahya ibn Hakim informed us of it, al-Hanafi informed us, Abdullah ibn Nafi' informed us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording. He said: He used to say when he sold: No khiyabah, meaning: No khilabah (no deceit)."
"5963","5959 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ali known as al-Kirmani narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah informed us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: Hibban ibn Munqidh had suffered a blow to his head which took away some of his reason, and when he sold or bought he would say: No deceit (la khilabah)."
"5964","5960 - Ali ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hushaym informed us, from Kawthar ibn Hakim, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed them from what you eat and clothe them from what you wear. And these words, we do not know them narrated from Ibn Umar except by this chain."
"5965","5961 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Aziz informed us, Kawthar ibn Hakim informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed wine, its presser, the one for whom it is pressed, its carrier, the one to whom it is carried, its seller, its buyer, its server, and its drinker, and he forbade its price to the Muslims."
"5966","5962 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah informed us, Sadaqah ibn Abdullah informed us, from Hashim ibn Zayd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever touches his private part, let him perform ablution."
"5967","5963 - Abdah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Umar ibn Habib informed us, Abdullah ibn Amir informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say twelve takbirs in the two Eid prayers, seven in the first and five in the last."
"5968","5964 - Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Quta'i narrated to us, al-Hajjaj informed us, Hammad informed us, from Jamil ibn Ziyad, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drinks wine, flog him three times; if he returns a fourth time, kill him. And this hadith is abrogated with respect to killing."
"5969","5965 - Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Abdullah informed us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah: that al-Nu'ayman was brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having drunk wine three times and he ordered that he be beaten; when the fourth time came he was brought having drunk and he was ordered to be flogged, and that abrogated killing."
"5970","5966 - Ahmad ibn Sinan al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Asadi informed us, Muti' al-A'war al-Ansari informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar; and from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar; and from Abu al-Zinad, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden."
"5971","5967 - And Ahmad ibn Sinan informed us of it, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim informed us, Abdullah ibn Umar informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, and Zayd ibn Aslam, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whatever intoxicates in large amount, its small amount is forbidden."
"5972","5968 - Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, Addal ibn Muhammad informed us, Muhammad ibn Juhadah informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Cupping on an empty stomach is best, in it is cure and blessing, it increases reason and increases the memorizer's memory, so be cupped in the name of Allah on Monday and Tuesday. Abu Bakr said: And he mentioned in the hadith something whose place I have not yet found, nor its completion."
"5973","5969 - And Umar ibn al-Khattab informed us of it, Abdullah ibn Salih informed us, Attaf ibn Khalid informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cupping on an empty stomach is best, in it is cure and blessing, it increases reason and increases the memorizer's memory; whoever is to be cupped, in the name of Allah let him be cupped on Thursday, and avoid cupping on Friday, Saturday, Sunday, Monday and Tuesday - meaning: be cupped in them - the day on which affliction was removed from Ayyub, meaning Tuesday; and avoid cupping on Wednesday, for it is a day on which a people were struck with affliction, and leprosy and vitiligo do not begin except on Wednesday or Wednesday night. Then Abdullah ibn Umar called a three-year-old child of his and kissed his mouth. And this hadith was only narrated by al-Attaf from Nafi', and al-Attaf's hadith was weakened only because of this hadith; and al-Addal ibn Muhammad is a Kufan shaykh not corroborated in this hadith from Ibn Juhadah, nor did Ibn Juhadah narrate from Nafi' any hadith other than this."
"5974","5970 - Umar ibn al-Khattab narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Attaf informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I did not pass by any heaven but the angels said: O Muhammad, command your ummah to use cupping, for the best of what you treat with is cupping, costus, and black seed. Abu Bakr said: al-Kust means al-qust (costus)."
"5975","5971 - Muhammad ibn Ma'mar narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Khattab informed us, Abu Ma'shar informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cheats us is not of us."
"5976","5972 - Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id informed us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar informed us, from Umar ibn Nafi', from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade qaza' (shaving part of the head and leaving part)."
"5977","5973 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qati'i informed us of it, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tufawi informed us, from Ayyub, from Umar ibn Nafi', from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording."
"5978","5974 - And Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna informed us of it, Uthman ibn Umar al-Ghatafani informed us, Umar ibn Nafi' informed us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): that he forbade qaza'."
"5979","5975 - Mu'ammal ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ibrahim informed us, Ali ibn al-Hakam informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade the stud fee of the stallion (payment for mating)."
"5980","5976 - And Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik informed us of it, Yazid ibn Zuray' informed us, Ali ibn al-Hakam informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording. And this hadith, we do not know anyone who narrates it from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except Ali ibn al-Hakam, and he is a famous man from Basra."
"5981","5977 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir informed us, Abdullah ibn Musa al-Taymi informed us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over al-Najashi and said four takbirs over him."
"5982","5978 - Ahmad ibn Thabit narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Kathir informed us, Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah informed us, from Qatadah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is passed in front of by someone, let him repel him; if he returns, let him repel him; if he returns, let him fight him, for he is Satan. And we do not know Qatadah narrated from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except this hadith, nor do we know anyone narrated it from Sa'id except al-Nadr ibn Kathir, and he is a famous man from Basra, there is no harm in him."
"5983","5979 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, Khazim Abu Muhammad al-Kufi informed us, Ata ibn al-Sa'ib informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The people of kindness in this world are the people of kindness in the Hereafter. And we do not know Ata ibn al-Sa'ib narrated from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, except this hadith, and we did not hear anyone narrate it from Khazim except Nasr ibn Ali."
"5984","5980 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Abu al-Mu'alla Sulayman ibn Muslim informed us, he said: I asked Sulayman al-Taymi: Does anyone come out of the Fire? He said: Nafi' narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: By Allah, none comes out of the Fire until he remains in it for ahqab (long ages). He said: And the hiqb is eighty-odd years, each year three hundred and sixty days of what you count."
"5985","5981 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Muslim informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, raised (to the Prophet): He said: The seal hangs from the leg of the Throne; when kinship complains, sins are committed, and boldness is shown toward Allah, Allah sends the seal and it seals his heart, and he comprehends nothing after that. And these two hadiths, we do not know anyone narrated them from al-Taymi, from Nafi', except Sulayman ibn Muslim, and he is a famous Basran."
"5986","5982 - Muhammad ibn Mirdas narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Muslim informed us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that a man asked him about the night prayer, and he said: Two by two, then one. And these hadiths, we do not know anyone narrated them from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Nafi', except Abu al-Mu'alla, and he is a man from Basra; as for two of them, we do not know them narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route: one is the hadith of the hiqb, and the other is the hadith of the seal; and as for the night prayer, none narrated it from al-Taymi, from Nafi', other than him. It is only narrated from Nafi' by other routes, and it is only known from al-Taymi, from Tawus, from Ibn Umar."
"5987","5983 - Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, my father informed me, Ibn Abi Dhi'b informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray the two rak'ahs after Maghrib except in his house, nor would he pray after Friday except in his house."
"5988","5984 - Abdullah ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja informed us, Sa'id ibn Salamah informed us, Abu Bakr, a man from the descendants of Abdullah ibn Umar, informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that a man passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was passing water, and the man greeted him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned the greeting to him, then said: I only returned the greeting to you because I feared you would say: I greeted him and he did not return to me; so if you see me like this, do not greet me, for I will not return the greeting to you."
"5989","5985 - And Muhammad ibn Yahya informed us of it, Abu Ahmad informed us, Sufyan informed us, from al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: that a man greeted the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was urinating, and he did not return the greeting to him."
"5990","5986 - And Nasr ibn Ali informed us, my father informed us, from Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I saw in a dream as if I were using the siwak with two men present, so I gave it to the younger, then it was said to me: Give precedence to the elder, so I handed it to the elder."
"5991","5987 - And Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, Ya'mar ibn Bishr narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak informed us, from Usamah ibn Zayd, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with similar wording. And he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, commanded me to give precedence to the elder."
"5992","5988 - Muhammad ibn Miskin narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yusuf informed us, Abdullah ibn Lahi'ah informed us, Khalid ibn Abi Imran informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays the Fajr prayer is under Allah's protection, so let none violate Allah regarding His protection; whoever violates Allah's protection, Allah will cast him face-down into the Fire."
"5993","5989 - Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Abd al-Hakam informed us, Bakr ibn Mudar informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, from Nafi' who said: Ibn Umar used to supplicate with these supplications, claiming that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with them: O Allah, apportion for us today of Your fear what will come between us and disobeying You, of Your obedience what will bring us to Your mercy, and of certainty what will make the calamities of this world light upon us; O Allah, grant us enjoyment of our sight and hearing, make them lasting for us, place our vengeance upon those who wronged us, grant us victory over those who oppose us, do not make our calamity in our religion, do not make this world our greatest concern, and do not give power over us to those who will not show us mercy. These words, we do not know them narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in this wording except by this route. And Ubaydullah ibn Zahr is weak in hadith, and only what he is alone in narrating is written from his hadith."
"5994","5990 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Karamah narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa informed us, Salim Abu Ghiyath informed us, from Matar, meaning al-Warraq, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: A man wearing travel clothes came until he sat before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed his hands on his knees, then said: What is Islam? He said: Bearing witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, praying the five prayers, fasting the month of Ramadan, paying zakat, and performing Hajj to the House. He said: If I do that, am I a Muslim? He said: You have spoken the truth. Then he said: What is faith? He said: Believing in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the Last Day, resurrection, reckoning, Paradise, Hell, and decree. He said: If I do that, am I a believer? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: What is ihsan? He said: Worshipping Allah as if you see Him; if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: If I do that, am I a muhsin? He said: Yes. He said: You have spoken the truth. He said: When is the Hour? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, the one asked about it knows no more than the questioner, but I will inform you of its signs: when you see the barefoot, naked - meaning the Arabs, I think he said - competing in building tall structures. He said: And he left, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bring the man to me. So we went out and saw no one. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is Jibril; he came to teach you your religion. He never came to me in such a form as today. And this hadith was narrated by Hammad ibn Zayd, from Matar, from Ibn Buraydah, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). And in the hadith of Salim, from Matar, there are two expressions differing from the hadith of Ibn Buraydah, so we mentioned it for that reason and clarified the defect in it."
"5995","5991 - Ali ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl informed us, my father narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, Abu Bakr was in a suburb of Medina. He said: He entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and placed his mouth on the forehead of the Messenger of Allah and kissed him, saying: May my father and mother be ransom for you; you were good alive and good dead. He said: When he came out, he passed by Umar who was saying: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah has not died, nor will he die until he kills the hypocrites. He said: They had rejoiced at the death of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and raised their heads. So Abu Bakr passed by him and said: O man, restrain yourself, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has died. Have you not heard Allah say: ""Indeed you will die and indeed they will die,"" and ""We did not grant immortality to any human before you; if you die, will they live forever?"" He said: And he came to the minbar, ascended it, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, if Muhammad was your god whom you worship, your god has died; and if your God is Allah who is in heaven, your God is alive and never dies. He said: Then he recited: ""Muhammad is but a messenger; messengers have passed before him,"" until he completed the verse. He said: Then he descended, and the believers rejoiced at that and their joy intensified, and gloom seized the hypocrites. Abdullah ibn Umar said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it was as if covers were over our faces and they were removed. And this hadith we only mentioned because Abu Bakr - may Allah have mercy on him - kissed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after he died. And we do not know anyone narrated this hadith from Fudayl except his son Muhammad ibn Fudayl."
"5996","5992 - Amr ibn Isa al-Duba'i narrated to us, Abd al-A'la ibn Abd al-A'la informed us, Ibrahim ibn Yazid informed us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah's anger is severe against a woman who brings into a people a child not of them, who looks upon their private matters and shares in their wealth. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except by this route with this chain; and Ibrahim ibn Yazid is weak in hadith, though a group narrated from him, among them al-Thawri and others, and what he is alone in narrating is written from his hadith."
"5997","5993 - al-Hasan ibn Arafah narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Bazi' Abu Abdullah informed us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman's travel with her slave is neglect. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this route, nor do we know anyone narrated from Bazi' except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"5998","5994 - Abdullah ibn Ahmad ibn Shabbawayh al-Marwazi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi Maryam informed us, Yahya ibn Ayyub informed us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar and A'ishah who both said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks a right, let him seek it with dignity, in full or not in full. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a better chain than this chain."
"5999","5995 - Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. And this hadith, we do not know it narrated from Ibn Umar except by this route with this chain; and al-Hakam is weak in hadith, though many narrated from him and tolerated his hadith."
"6000","5996 - Ahmad ibn Ishaq and al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both said: Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr informed us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad informed us, from Musa ibn Jubayr, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he heard the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When Allah sent Adam down to earth, the angels said: O Lord, ""Will You place in it one who corrupts in it and sheds blood, while we glorify You with praise and sanctify You? He said: Indeed I know what you do not know."" They said: We are more obedient to You than the children of Adam. So Allah, blessed and exalted, said to the angels: Choose two angels from among the angels to descend to earth and We shall see how they act. They said: Our Lord, Harut and Marut. So they descended to earth, and al-Zuharah appeared to them as a woman of the most beautiful people. She came to them and they asked her for herself. She said: No, by Allah, until you associate partners with Allah, or words to that effect. They said: By Allah, we will never associate anything with Allah. She went away from them, then returned carrying an infant boy, and they asked her for herself. She said: No, by Allah, until you kill this boy. They said: No, by Allah, we will never kill him. She went away, then returned carrying a cup of wine, and they asked her for herself. She said: No, by Allah, until you drink this wine. So they drank, became intoxicated, fell upon her, and killed the boy. When they sobered up, the woman said: By Allah, you left nothing of what you had refused except you did it when you became intoxicated. So they were given the choice of the punishment of this world and the punishment of the Hereafter, and they chose the punishment of this world. And this hadith was narrated by others than Musa ibn Jubayr, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, stopped (mawquf). And Musa ibn Jubayr, there is no harm in him; the raising of this hadith, in my view, comes only from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad."
